hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Buqay bin Mukhlid, may God Almighty have mercy on him, narrated to me, saying: Abu Bakr, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah, narrated to us, saying:\n\n(1) Hashim bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, When God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the bathroom, he said: I seek refuge in God from wickedness and evil things. (Bukhari 142, 6322. Abu Dawud 4.5)"
"2","(2) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Qasim al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This crowd is dying, so if one of you enters the private room, let him say: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from evil and evil things. (Nasa’i 9905. Ibn Majah 296)"
"3","(3) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Omar, who said: Al-Hasan bin Muslim bin Yannaq narrated to me, on the authority of a man From the companions of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: Abdullah said: If you go to the toilet and want to uncover yourself, say: O God, I seek refuge in You. Of the unclean abomination, the wickedness and evil things, and the accursed Satan."
"4","(4) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: When Hudhaifi entered the private room, he said: I seek refuge By God, from the unclean uncleanness, the evil one, the accursed Satan."
"5","(5) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, and he is Najih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet When he entered the shroud, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he would say: In the name of God, O God, I seek refuge in You from wickedness and evil things. (Tabarani 357)"
"6","(6) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of al-Zabarqan al-Abdi, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, who said: When you enter a private room, say: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the unclean, the vile, the vile, the accursed Satan."
"7","(7) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, he said: Israel told us, he said: Yusuf bin Abi Burda told us, he said: I heard my father saying: I entered upon Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and I heard her saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he comes out of the stool, he says: Your forgiveness. (Ibn Majah 3000, An-Nasa’i 9907)"
"8","(8) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi. When Noah the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out of the stool, he would say: Praise be to God who has removed harm from him. And He healed me."
"9","(9) Hushaym narrated to us, he said: The common people informed us, he said: I narrated, that Noah used to say: Praise be to God who made me taste. its pleasure, keep its benefit in me, and remove its harm from me. (Bayhaqi 4469)"
"10","(10) Abd ibn Sulaiman and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ali; That Abu Dharr used to say when he left the toilet: Praise be to God who has removed harm from me and healed me. (Tabarani 372)"
"11","(11) Abdi told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Hudhayfy used to say when he went out, meaning from the privates: Praise be to God who removed harm from me and healed me."
"12","(12) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zam`a, on the authority of Salama bin Wahram, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : When one of you goes out of the bathroom, let him say: Praise be to God, who has removed from me that which hurts me, and has kept away from me that which hurts me. It benefits me. (Tabarani 371, Dar Qatni 1/57)"
"13","(13) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said, Huraim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, he said: Abu When the Darda comes out of the toilet, he says: Praise be to God, who has removed harm from me and healed me."
"14","(14) Zayd ibn al-Hubab and Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd. He said: Rabih narrated to me. Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abi Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of God upon him. (Tabarani 380. Ahmad 3/41)"
"15","(15) Affan told us, he said: Wahhab told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala told us, that he heard Abu Thifal speaking, He heard Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Huwaytab saying: My grandmother told me, she heard her father. He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There is no prayer for one who has not performed ablution, and there is no ablution for one who has not mentioned it. The name of God be upon him. (Tirmidhi 25, 26. Ibn Majah 398)"
"16","(16) Abdū narrated to us, on the authority of Haritha, on the authority of Amrā, she said: I asked Aisha: What was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God bless him and grant him peace? She said: Whenever he performed ablution and put his hand in the water, he would say the name of God and perform the ablution, and he would complete the ablution.\n(Tabarani 383. Ibn Majah 1062)"
"17","(17) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hussein bin Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr, who said: If a servant performs ablution, So he mentioned the name of God when he took his ablution, his entire body was pure, and if he performed ablution and did not mention the name of God, he did not It is purified from it, except what gets on it with water."
"18","(18) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: He pronounces the name of God when he performs ablution, but if he does not do that, then that is sufficient."
"19","(19) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim al-Wasiti, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: Whoever says when he has finished his ablution: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, I bear witness that no There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You. It was sealed with a seal, then raised under the Throne, and has not been broken to this day. Resurrection\n(Nasa’i 9910. Tabarani 391)"
"20","(20) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abdullah bin Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja'd, he said: When Ali had finished his ablution, he would say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant. And His Messenger, my Lord, make me among those who repent, and make me among those who purify themselves."
"21","(21) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’i ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris. Al-Khawlani, and Abu Uthman, on the authority of Jubayr ibn Nufayr ibn Malik al-Hadrami, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir al-Junai, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No one performs ablution and performs it well, then prays two rak’ahs, coming forward. With his heart and face, except that Paradise becomes necessary for him. He said: Then Omar said: There was no one before her more than her, as if you had come before? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs ablution and says: I bear witness that there is no god but God, alone with no partner, I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Eight gates of Paradise were opened for him, and he may enter whichever way he wishes. (Muslim 210. Tirmidhi 55)"
"22","(22) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Nakha’i narrated to me, on the authority of Zayd al-Ammi, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs ablution and says: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and He alone does not your partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, three times, the gates of Paradise were opened for him eight times, and he enters. Whoever he wants\n(Ibn Majah 469. Ahmad 3/265)"
"23","(23) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Manyal, that Abu Al-Aaliyah saw a man performing ablution, so when When he finished, he said: O God, make me among those who repent, and make me among those who purify themselves. Then he said: Purification with water is good, but they Those who are cleansed of sins."
"24","(24) Al-Muqri’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Zurah bin Ma’bad Abu Aqeel narrated to me that a cousin He informed him that he heard Uqba bin Amir say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs ablution and completes it. his ablution, then he raised his head to the heavens and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone with no partner, and that Muhammad His servant and Messenger, eight gates of Paradise were opened for him, and he may enter whichever one he wishes. (Ahmad 4/150 and Tabarani 17/916)"
"25","(25) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: When Hudhafi purified himself, he said: I bear witness that There is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Oh God, make me among those who repent, and make me among those who purify themselves."
"26","(26) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaida (h), and Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, both on the authority of Simak bin Harb, On the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No prayer will be accepted except with ritual purity, and no Truth from deceit.\n(Muslim 1/204, Ibn Majah 272)"
"27","(27) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ibn Sinan, on the authority of Anas, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Sadaqah will not be accepted from fraudulent people, nor prayer will be accepted without purification. (Ibn Majah 273)"
"28","(28) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala narrated to us, that he heard Abu Thifal speaking, He said: I heard Rabah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Sufyan bin Huwaytib saying: My grandmother told me that she heard her father. He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There is no prayer for one who does not perform ablution. \n(Tirmidhi 25, 26. Ibn Majah 398)"
"29","(29) Shababah bin Suwar and Ubaid bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shubabi, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of His father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: God does not accept a prayer without purity, nor charity from a deceitful person.\n(Abu Dawud 60. Ibn Majah 271)"
"30","(30) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Adam bin Ali, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Some people will call those who are deficient on the Day of Judgment. Resurrection, and a man said: Who is Abu Abdul Rahman? He said: One of them was lacking in his purity, and he was distracted in his prayer."
"31","(31) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah said: It will not be accepted. Prayer except by purification."
"32","(32) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muja’ bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: His prayer will not be accepted. Without purity."
"33","(33) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of al-Mustarid ibn al-Ahnaf, he said: Omar said: No prayer will be accepted without purification."
"34","(34) Ubaidah bin Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Ruh, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, so he recited a Roman surah and hesitated over it. When he left, he said: He only confuses our prayers. A people who attend the prayer without purifying themselves. Whoever attends the prayer should purify himself well. (Ahmad 3/471, An-Nasa’i 1019)"
"35","(35) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: No one maintains the ritual purity except a believer.\n\n(Ibn Majah 2777, Ahmad 5/276)"
"36","(36) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: No one will perform ablution except a believer. (Ibn Majah 278)"
"37","(37) Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, on the authority of Abi Salam, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: Birds are part of faith.\n(Ahmad 5/342, Bayhaqi 1/42)"
"38","(38) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Layla al-Kindi, on the authority of Hijr Ibn Adiyy said: Ali told us that birds are part of faith."
"39","(39) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If a Muslim man performs ablution, his sins are removed from his hearing, sight, hands and feet. If he sits, he will sit forgiven. (Ahmad 5/252)"
"40","(40) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I said, O Messenger of God How do you know who among your nation you have not seen? He said: They are gray-faced, stained from the effects of ablution. (Ahmad 1/452)"
"41","(41) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father used to say: Ablution is half of the prayer."
"42","(42) Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Harry, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: You will return to me, covered with turbidity from ablution. The features of your nation are not For someone else (Ibn Majah 4282 and Abu Ali 6181)"
"43","(43) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Yazid bin Talq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Bilamani, on the authority of Amr bin Absa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When a servant performs ablution, he washes His sins fall from his hand, and when he washes his face, his sins fall from his face, and when he washes his arms and wiped his head, his sins fell from his arms and his head, and when he washed his feet, his sins fell from His legs (Ibn Majah 283)"
"44","(44) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Shall I not guide you to Something through which God expiates sins and increases good deeds? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Performing ablution thoroughly in times of hardship, and taking many steps to these mosques. (Ibn Majah 427, Abu Ali 1350)"
"45","(45) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Kathir ibn Mudarrak, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Yazid He said: Abdullah said: The expiations are completing the ablution with sabras, moving the feet to the Friday prayers, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer."
"46","(46) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah, who said: I heard Humran saying: I used to add perfume to Uthman. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us: There is no man who performs ablution and does it well, but his sins are forgiven. And between the last prayer. (Muslim 1/207)"
"47","(47) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Yazid bin Bishr, he said: God revealed to Moses that Perform ablution, and if you do not do it and a calamity befalls you, then have no one to blame but yourself."
"48","(48) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of al-Dahhak; In the Almighty’s saying: (And stand obedient to God), He said: Obedient to God in ablution. (Al-Baqarah Verse 238)"
"49","(49) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Othman bin Hakim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, on the authority of Hamran, he said: I heard Othman He says: Whoever performs ablution well and performs it well and completes it, his sins will leave his body until they come out from under him. Nails (Muslim 1/216)"
"50","(50) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Salma bin Sabra, on the authority of Salman, who said: If a Muslim man performs ablution, His sins were placed on his head and opened, just as the stem of a palm tree is opened. (Ibn Hibban 4/317)"
"51","(51) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Salma bin Sabra, on the authority of Salman, the same."
"52","(52) Qubaisa bin Uqba narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: I was with Salman took a branch from a withered tree and opened it, then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Who He performed ablution and performed it well, and his sins fell apart like a piece of paper. (Ahmad 437, vol. 5, Tabarani 6151)"
"53","(53) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Abu Ghataif, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Whoever performs ablution in purity, ten good deeds will be recorded for him."
"54","(54) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Hayya, who said: I saw Ali performing ablution and cleansing his palms. Then he washed his face three times, and his arms three times, and wiped his head, then washed his feet up to the ankles, then he got up and drank. He failed to perform his ablution, then he said: I only wanted to show you the purification of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 117. Tirmidhi 48)"
"55","(55) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Ali, who said: He performed ablution, rinsed his mouth three times, and sniffed the water. He took three from one palm and washed his face three times, then he put his hand into the rak’ah and wiped his head and washed his feet, then he said: This is the ablution of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Khuzaymah 147 and Ibn Hibban 1056)"
"56","(56) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, on the authority of Hamran, He said: Othman called for water, performed ablution, then laughed, and said: Don’t you ask me why I laughed? They said: O Commander of the Faithful, what made you laugh? He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution as I did. He rinsed his mouth, sniffed his mouth, and washed his face three times. He held his hands three times, and wiped his head and the backs of his feet. (Ahmed 258, Volume 1)"
"57","(57) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution, washed his face three times, his hands twice, and wiped his head and feet. Twice (Bukhari 1851, Muslim 211)"
"58","(58) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Find it; That a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about ablution? So he called for water and performed ablution three times, then said: This is the way of purification. Whoever increases or decreases has transgressed or done wrong. (ابوداؤد ۱۳۶، جلد۲)"
"59","(59) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bint Mu’awiz bin Afra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us, and we put the ablution for him, and he performed ablution three times and wiped his head."
"60","(60) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan bin Uqba al-Muradi, Abu Kibran, who said: I heard Abd Khair al-Hamdani say Ali said: Shall I not show you the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Then he performed ablution three times."
"61","(61) Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Sami’, on the authority of Abu In front of him; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution, washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth and nose three times, and performed ablution. Three, three, three. (Ahmad 258, vol. 5. Tabarani 7990)"
"62","(62) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Abu Anas; Othman performed ablution while sitting, and said: Shall I not show you the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Then he performed ablution for us three times. (Dar Qatni 11. Muslim 9)"
"63","(63) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Aamir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Uthman; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution three times."
"64","(64) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed ablution, took several scoops, rinsed some of it and rinsed it out, then took several scoops and washed himself. He faced him, then he scooped a scoop and washed his right hand, then he scooped a scoop and washed his left hand, then he scooped a scoop and washed his left hand. He touched his head and ears inside them with his index fingers, and with his thumbs he moved toward the back of his ears and wiped their insides. He looked at them, then he went back to back and washed his right foot, then he went back to back and washed his left foot. (Ibn Majah 439. An-Nasa’i 105)"
"65","(65) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; Othman performed ablution three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet, then said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He performed ablution."
"66","(66) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: I told him: I narrated on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Did he perform ablution several times? He said: Yes. (Ibn Majah 410, Dar Qatni 8)"
"67","(67) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Quraysh, who said: We led Omar to Sarraar, so he performed ablution and washed himself. Twice \n(Ibn Saad 7)"
"68","(68) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Qardha, who said, I heard Omar say: The ablution is performed in three days. Three and two are sufficient."
"69","(69) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Omar, who said: Concerning rinsing the mouth, sniffing the nose, and washing the face. Washing the hands and feet two times is sufficient, and three times is better."
"70","(70) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Muslim bin Subaih, who said: I saw Ibn Umar performing ablution. Three times, then he wiped his head and ears."
"71","(71) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, who said: I saw Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla performing ablution, rinsing his mouth and sniffing myrrh. Or twice, and he washed his face three times, and his arms three times, and wiped his head and washed his feet three times, and did not He showed him his beard, then said: This is how I saw Ali performing ablution."
"72","(72) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muslim, who said: I saw Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla. He performed ablution three times."
"73","(73) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ismail bin Ibrahim, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas He performed ablution in Dar al-Nadwah several times."
"74","(74) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution one by one."
"75","(75) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, that Omar performed ablution twice. Amir said: And Abu did it. Early"
"76","(76) Waki’ and Al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I saw Salim bin Abdullah He performed ablution several times."
"77","(77) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will suffice you from Ablution is done twice, and if you do it three times, then you have done it properly."
"78","(78) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Ablution is Witr."
"79","(79) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri how many ablutions are sufficient for The face and arms? He said: I do not see one single word except that it is sufficient. He said: So I said to him: Indeed, Maymun says: Three on the front and three on the back. The arms! He said: This is the most effective ablution."
"80","(80) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Jariri informed us, on the authority of Urwah bin Qubaysah, on the authority of a man from the Ansar, On the authority of his father; Othman said: Shall I not show you what the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was like? They said: Yes, so he called for water and rinsed his mouth three times, and blew his nose three times, and washed his face three times, and his arms three times, and wiped his head. And he washed his feet, then he said: And know that the two ears are from the head, then he said: I have sought, or I have sought for you, the ablution of the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 61, Volume 1, Dar Qatni 104)"
"81","(81) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution twice. \n(Abu Dawud 137 Tirmidhi 43)"
"82","(82) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Ablution is performed once, twice, or thrice."
"83","(83) Waki’ told us, he said, Dawud bin Qais told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Maqsim, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: As for who was He performs ablution well every once in a while."
"84","(84) Yahya bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit bin Sabria, on the authority of his father, He said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about ablution? He said: Perform ablution thoroughly, pass between your fingers, and inhale frequently, unless you are fasting. (Ibn Majah 448. Abu Dawud 143)"
"85","(85) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Waqid, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, who said: Omar passed by a people performing ablution, and he said: Let them pick it up."
"86","(86) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Miskin, on the authority of Huzayl, who said: Abdullah said: Let the man settle what is between Fingers with water, or let them be covered with fire. (Abdul Razzaq 68)"
"87","(87) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: He narrated to me someone who heard Hudhayfi say: Mix between the fingers. Perform ablution before fire engulfs it."
"88","(88) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Ata, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas performing ablution and washing his feet until he traced between his fingers and washed them."
"89","(89) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Shayba ibn Nisah, who said: I accompanied al-Qasim ibn Muhammad to Mecca. So I saw him, when he performed ablution for prayer, inserting the fingers of his hand between the toes of his feet. He said: And he was pouring water. Ali, so I said to him: O Abu Muhammad, why are you doing this? He said: I saw Abdullah bin Omar making it."
"90","(90) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He saw him on a journey taking off his socks, then interlacing his fingers."
"91","(91) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Mix between your fingers with water Before the fire fills it. (Tabarani 9213)"
"92","(92) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abdullah, with a similar hadith of Ibn Namer"
"93","(93) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: When you perform ablution, start with your fingers and mix them. It used to be said: It is the abode of Satan."
"94","(94) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, who said: I saw Ibn al-Hanafiyy performing ablution, crossing his fingers."
"95","(95) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Mix your fingers with water, do not mix them with fire. Very little remains."
"96","(96) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: You will Your fingers in water, or God will mix them with fire."
"97","(97) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Wasil bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Sura, on the authority of his uncle Abu Ayyub, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Those who are pickled have preferred that you mix water between your fingers, and that you pickle food. (Tabarani 4061, Ahmad 416, vol. 5)"
"98","(98) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Hassan bin Bilal, who said: I saw Ammar bin Yasser performing ablution. So he trimmed his beard, so I said to him? He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do it. (Tirmidhi 30, Ibn Majah 429)"
"99","(99) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas combing his beard when he performed ablution."
"100","(100) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to comb his beard."
"101","(101) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’n, who said: I saw a man performing ablution and combing his beard."
"102","(102) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to comb his beard when he performed ablution."
"103","(103) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr performing ablution and combing his beard."
"104","(104) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Mu’alla ibn Jabir, on the authority of Al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I saw Ibn Umar combing his beard."
"105","(105) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Nadr ibn Ma’bad, who said: I saw Abu Qulabab, when he performed ablution, he put it through his beard."
"106","(106) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqqashi. On the authority of Anas; When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed ablution, he would ruffle his beard. (Ibn Majah 431, Ibn Saad 386)"
"107","(107) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Mujahid; He used to comb his beard when he performed ablution."
"108","(108) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin performing ablution and combing his beard."
"109","(109) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Ibn Sirin used to analyze it."
"110","(110) Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: I saw him. He pickles his beard."
"111","(111) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of a man he did not name; That Ali passed by a man who was performing ablution, and he said: His beard is broken."
"112","(112) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Sulaym Al-Baili, he said: Abu Ghalib narrated to me, he said: I said to my father in front of him: Tell us about the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He performed ablution three times, mixed his beard, and said: This is what I saw. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does so."
"113","(113) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Aamir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: I saw Othman He performed ablution and mixed his beard three times, and said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do it. (Ibn Hibban 1081. Tirmidhi) 31)"
"114","(114) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Haytham ibn Jamaz, on the authority of Yazid ibn Aban, on the authority of Anas; On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Gabriel came to me and said: When you perform ablution, rinse your beard."
"115","(115) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When he performed ablution, he would let it through his beard."
"116","(116) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said, Hassan bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Ibrahim; He performed ablution and combed his beard."
"117","(117) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id al-Zubaidi, who said: I asked Ibrahim: Should I soak my beard with water? Or is what happened to her enough? He said: What happened to her is sufficient for her."
"118","(118) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Al-Hassan did not do it, meaning he did not comb his beard."
"119","(119) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: I saw him wiping my side. His beard and his head, but he did not touch them."
"120","(120) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, he said: What he asked is sufficient for you. From your face to your beard."
"121","(121) Waki` told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thawair, who said: I saw Abu Ja`far not combing his beard."
"122","(22) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, Muhammad bin Ali, Mujahid, and Al-Qasim; They used to wipe their beards, but they did not comb them."
"123","(123) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, he said: I saw him. He performed ablution, and I did not see him through his beard. Then he said: This is how I saw Ali performing ablution."
"124","(124) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: What is shed on your face on your beard is sufficient for you. And do not disturb it."
"125","(125) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ajlan, who said: Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad was asked about dyeing the beard? He said: I don't have to worry about it."
"126","(126) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I saw Ibrahim performing ablution and he did not Her beard"
"127","(127) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: If you are able to reach the roots of the beard with water, do so."
"128","(128) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I saw him washing his beard, so I said: To him: Is it Sunnah to wash the beard? He said: No."
"129","(129) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Indeed, he saw that its roots were from the water, meaning the beard."
"130","(130) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. And Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim; They both liked to wipe the inside of the beard during ablution."
"131","(131) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: When you perform ablution, do not forget to perform it."
"132","(132) Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Shubramah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: What is the matter with the man? He washes his beard before it grows, but when it grows he does not wash it!"
"133","(133) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, performed ablution and wiped his head. (Ibn Majah 435)"
"134","(134) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamran, on the authority of Uthman, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace."
"135","(135) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to perform ablution three times, except for wiping once in a while."
"136","(136) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to wipe the His head once."
"137","(137) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar used to wipe his mouth repeatedly."
"138","(138) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I entered upon Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, so he called for ablution, performed ablution, wiped his head once, and washed his feet three times. He said: This is how I saw Ali. He performs ablution."
"139","(139) Sharik told us, on the authority of Sinan al-Bajli, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Wiping the head is sufficient."
"140","(140) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that he used to wipe his head. Three."
"141","(141) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd Rabb bin Ayman, who said: I said to Ata’: Would it suffice for me to wipe my head? He said: Yes."
"142","(142) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thuwayr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If I were on the shore of the Euphrates I did not add anything to my anointing."
"143","(143) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about wiping the head? They said: bitterly."
"144","(144) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid ibn Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim wiping his head once."
"145","(145) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, he said: Al-Rabi’ narrated to me. He said: She said: He came to us. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution and wiped his head twice. (Abu Dawud 127 Tirmidhi 33)"
"146","(146) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi`, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: He used to order that the head be wiped over and over again."
"147","(147) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Sayegh, on the authority of Ata, that he said: He wipes The head once."
"148","(148) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wiped his head several times. One"
"149","(149) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, and Zazan, And easy; When they performed ablution, they would wipe their heads three times."
"150","(150) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He performed ablution and wiped his head like this. Hafs ordered his hand over his head until he wiped the back of it.\n(Ahmad 481, Abu Dawud 133)"
"151","(151) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, saying: I said to Hamid: When Anas bin Malik wiped his head, would he ruffle his hair? He said: No."
"152","(152) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, that he was He wipes his head like this, from the front to the back, then returns his hand to the front."
"153","(153) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, he said: Al-Rabi’ narrated to me, she said: It was The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us and many times. She said: So we put the water for him, so he came to us and performed ablution. He wiped his head, starting with the back of it, then returned his hand to the forelock."
"154","(154) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar used to wipe his head like this, and Ayyub placed He placed it in the middle of his head, then placed it on the front of his head."
"155","(155) Hammad bin Masadi told us, on the authority of Zaid, who said: Salama used to wipe the front of his head."
"156","(156) Waki` bin al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever performs ablution, let him rinse his mouth and nose, while keeping his ears close to his head. (Dar Qatni 15)"
"157","(157) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and al-Hasan. They said: The two ears are among the The head"
"158","(158) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The ears are from the head."
"159","(159) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The ears are from the head."
"160","(160) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The ears are from the head."
"161","(161) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim. On the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab and al-Hasan, they said: The ears are from the head."
"162","(162) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: The ears are from the head."
"163","(163) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Hilal bin Asama, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The ears are from the head."
"164","(164) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to wipe his ears, And he says: They are from the head."
"165","(165) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: What is more beautiful than the ears is more beautiful than the face, and what Turn back and from the head."
"166","(166) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to wash his ears along with his face, and wipe them along with his head."
"167","(167) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The ears are from the head."
"168","(168) Abd al-Hamid bin Abd al-Rahman al-Hammani told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, He said: The ears are from the head."
"169","(169) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Urwah ibn Qubaysah, on the authority of a man from the Ansar, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Uthman, said: And know that the ears are from the head."
"170","(170) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I asked him about wiping the ears with the head, or with the head. The face? He said: With all of them."
"171","(171) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, who said: I saw a man performing ablution, and he started wiping the outside of his ears. And their insides, so I looked at it, and he said: Ibn Masoud used to order that."
"172","(172) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Saar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wiped his ears, the inside of them with his index fingers, and crossed them with his thumb to The outside of his ears, and he wiped the inside and the outside of them."
"173","(173) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he performed ablution, he would enter The two fingers that circled the thumbs were in his ears, so he wiped the inside of them and crossed the outside of them with the thumbs.\n(Abdul Razzaq 29)"
"174","(174) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, and Ibrahim, that they They said about the ears: Wipe the outside and the inside of them."
"175","(175) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Uthman, who said: He was one of his servants Ibn Al-Zubair, he said: I performed ablution on Ibn Umar and saw him wiping the back of his ears."
"176","(176) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Sila’, on the authority of Abd Khayr, who said: We were with Ali one day in prayer. Lunch, when he left, he called the boy for the basin, performed ablution, then put his fingers in his ears, then said to us: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution."
"177","(177) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, that Omar bin Al-Khattab performed ablution and inserted his fingers into the inside and outside of his ears, then wiped them."
"178","(178) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I saw Ikrimah wiping his feet, and he was saying this."
"179","(179) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say that it is wiping on the feet, and he used to say: He wipes the outside of them and the inside of them."
"180","(180) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Two washings and two wipes. (Abdul Razzaq 55)"
"181","(181) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It is wiping on the feet. Don’t you see that what was If he had to wash himself, tayammum was made obligatory for him, and if he did not have to wipe, he neglected it, so tayammum was not made obligatory for him."
"182","(182) Ismail Ibn Aliya narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Whenever Anas wiped his feet, it would become wet."
"183","(183) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Ali, who said: If religion were based on opinion The soles of the feet were more deserving of wiping than the outsides of the feet, but I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping They are visible (Ahmad 1/737)"
"184","(184) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Zubaid al-Yami, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, he said: Gabriel descended By wiping on the feet."
"185","(185) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: Gabriel came down with the anointing. (Ibn Jarir 129)"
"186","(186) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked Al-Aswad: Was it Omar washes his feet? He said: Yes, he used to wash them thoroughly."
"187","(187) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid; Anas used to wash his feet and legs until the water ran out."
"188","(188) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Alaqa, on the authority of Ibn Ghuraba’a; Omar bin Al-Khattab saw a man who washed the outside of his feet and left the insides of them, and he said: Why did you leave them to the fire?"
"189","(189) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Wash the feet until The Kaabain"
"190","(190) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If I I will pour water on him and he will wash his feet."
"191","(191) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saleh, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahhaf, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I heard him say: The Sunnah came from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace and the Muslims, meaning washing the feet."
"192","(192) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Hayya, who said: I saw Ali performing ablution and washing his feet. Al-Kaabin, and said: I wanted to show you the purification of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"193","(193) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he recited: {And your feet} meaning: It's back to ghusl."
"194","(194) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that he used to recite: {So wash your faces. And your hands to the elbows, and wipe your in-holes and your feet and your feet.} He says: The matter returns to washing."
"195","(195) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The matter returned to washing."
"196","(196) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {So wash your faces and your hands}, he said: That washing is rubbing."
"197","(197) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He was washing his feet."
"198","(198) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, he said: Al-Rabi’ told me, she said, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us, so he performed ablution and washed his feet three times."
"199","(199) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ruh bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Mu’awwidh Ibn Afraa, she said: Ibn Abbas came to me and asked me about this hadith. She means the hadith she mentioned, that she saw Did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution, and did he wash his feet? She said: Ibn Abbas said: People refuse anything except washing, and I do not find anything in the Book of God except wiping. (Ahmad 6/358, Hamidi 342)"
"200","(200) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Mahmoud, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw May God bless him and grant him peace. A blind man was performing ablution. He washed his face and hands, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made He said: The soles of your feet, so he started washing the soles of your feet. (Abdul Razzaq 77)"
"201","(201) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I told him: I caught one of them wiping On the feet? He said: Hadith."
"202","(202) Hammad bin Masadi told us, on the authority of Yazid, the client of Salama; He was washing his feet."
"203","(203) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala’, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; He used to wipe the head three times, taking water separately for each wipe."
"204","(204) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of his leaders, he said: I asked him? He said: Ali bin Abi Talib used to take water for his head. He said: I asked Hammad and he said: He should take water for his head."
"205","(205) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He used to take water to wipe the body. His head"
"206","(206) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: I saw Al-Qasim performing ablution, and he took fresh water for his head."
"207","(207) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to add water to wipe the head."
"208","(208) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went one by one and wiped his head and ears."
"209","(209) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He used to take fresh water for his head."
"210","(210) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Musab bin Sa’d, who said: Take water for your head. New"
"211","(211) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Waqid, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, who said: Take fresh water for your head."
"212","(212) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, who said: Al-Rabi’ bint Mu’awiz bin Afraa said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us, performed ablution, and wiped his head with what was left of his ablution."
"213","(213) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father. And on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Indeed, they were wiping their heads with the grace of their hands."
"214","(214) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He was wiping his head thanks to his ablution."
"215","(215) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he forgets to wipe his head, he There was wetness in his beard, so he mentioned while he was praying. If there was wetness in his beard, then let him wipe his head."
"216","(216) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he forgot to wipe his head, he found His beard is wet, it is sufficient for him to wipe his head with it."
"217","(217) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan. And on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"218","(218) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In his saying: Concerning a man who mentioned during prayer that he had not wiped his head and there was wetness in his beard. He said: He wiped off any wetness from his head. His beard"
"219","(219) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, as far as Hammad knows, on the authority of Ali He said: If a man performed ablution and forgot to wipe his head and found wetness in his beard, he took some of his beard and wiped his head."
"220","(220) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ajra, On the authority of Bilal; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped over the socks and the veil. (Tabarani 1060; Ibn Khuzaymah 180)"
"221","(221) Ismail Ibn Aliyah and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Usayla Al-Sanabihi, who said: I saw Abu Bakr wiping over me. The veil"
"222","(222) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his father; That Abu Musa came out of the toilet and wiped over his hood."
"223","(223) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: I saw Abu Imamah wiping over the turban."
"224","(224) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salama; She was wiping over the veil."
"225","(225) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I saw a man wiping over his socks and turbans."
"226","(226) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, who said: Omar said: If If you wish, wipe over the turban, and if you wish, remove it."
"227","(227) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, on the authority of Nabata, He said: I asked Omar bin Al-Khattab about wiping over the turban? He said: If you want, wipe over it, and if you want, then no."
"228","(228) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tariq, who said: I saw Hakim bin Jabir wiping over the turban."
"229","(229) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Shuraih, on the authority of Abu A Muslim client of Zaid bin Suhan said: I was with Salman and he saw a man taking off his socks to perform ablution, and Salman said to him: Wipe over your socks, your veil, and your forelocks, for I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping over The socks and the veil. (Ahmad 5/439, Ibn Majah 563)"
"230","(230) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, on the authority of his father, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped the front of his head and wiped over the turban. (Muslim 83. Tirmidhi 100)"
"231","(231) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Ja’far bin Amr bin Umayyah Al-Dhamri, on the authority of his father, said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping over his socks. And the turban. (Ibn Majah 562. Ahmad 4/139)"
"232","(232) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abbad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah Ibn Muhammad Ibn Ammar Ibn Yasir, He said: I asked Jabir about wiping over the turban? He said: The water touched the hair."
"233","(233) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi` ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Labid, who said: I saw Ali go to the bathroom. He was wearing a mule of his own, and he was wearing a lower garment, a robe, a turban, and slippers. I saw him urinating, then he performed ablution and unbuttoned the turban, so I saw His head is like the palm of your hand, with hair on him like the line of your fingers. So he wiped over his head, then he wiped over his socks."
"234","(234) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not wipe over the turban."
"235","(235) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: It was when Abraham had a turban or a hood on him. He raised it, then wiped his mouth."
"236","(236) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: I saw Al-Sha’abi perform ablution and uncover his turban."
"237","(237) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that he used to remove the turban. And he wipes his head with water."
"238","(238) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution. So he lifted the turban and wiped the front of his head."
"239","(239) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: Al-Qasim did not wipe over the turban, he used to remove his hair from his head. Then he wipes over it."
"240","(240) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man wipes on his forelock and on his turban."
"241","(241) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Amr ibn Wahhab al-Thaqafi, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn His people; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution, wiped his forelocks, and wiped over his turban. (Ahmad 4/249, An-Nasa’i 112)"
"242","(242) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The woman and the man are in Wiping the head is the same."
"243","(243) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I saw Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid performing ablution. So she put her hand under her veil and wiped it with her forelocks."
"244","(244) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: You enter A woman has her hand under her veil and wipes it with her forelocks."
"245","(245) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: She wipes her private parts."
"246","(246) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A woman should wipe her forelocks and tops, if she is She was anointed for the morning."
"247","(247) Abd al-Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; In the mirror, if she wants to wipe her head, he said: She puts her hand under the veil and wipes the front of her head. That will be sufficient. About her"
"248","(248) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima ibn al-Mundhir; She used to wipe over the naked, and she was close to the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"249","(249) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Khalid Khalid bin Dinar; Abu Al-Aaliyah was asked: How does a woman wipe her head? So he said to his wife: Tell her, and she said: Thus, and she passed her hand over the side of her head and wiped it."
"250","(250) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salama; She was wiping over the veil."
"251","(251) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: He was asked about a woman wiping over her veil? He said: No, but she should wipe over her head."
"252","(252) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a woman performs ablution, she should remove her veil. And let her wipe her head."
"253","(253) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A woman wipes on her forelock and on her veil."
"254","(254) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: Hammad said: A woman takes off her veil at every turn. Ablution"
"255","(255) Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father; Omar had a pot in which he heated water."
"256","(256) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father; Omar had a pot in which he heated water. (Dar Qatni 1)"
"257","(257) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I asked Nafi’ about hot water? He said: Ibn Omar used to perform ablution with an intimate bath."
"258","(258) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, who said: It is purified with water. It is cooked with fire, and when I perform ablution with hot water, I mix it with it."
"259","(259) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Abbas said: We condemn With oil that was cooked over the fire, and we perform ablution with hot water that was boiled over the fire."
"260","(260) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, he said: I asked Al-Hasan about performing ablution with hot water? He said: There is no harm in it."
"261","(261) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Badr, who said: I came to Abu Wael on the day of Jumu’ah, and he was heating water for him."
"262","(262) Hammad bin Masada told us, on the authority of Zaid, that Salama used to heat water for himself and perform ablution with it."
"263","(263) Qasim bin Malik told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked performing ablution with hot water."
"264","(264) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Abu Zayd, the servant of Amr ibn Harith, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him on the night of the jinn: Do you have birds? He said: No, except some wine as a treatment. He said: Good dates and pure water. (Ahmad 1/402, Abu Dawud 85)"
"265","(265) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, that he did not see any harm. By performing ablution with wine."
"266","(266) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Wine is ablution. For those who did not find water."
"267","(267) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah; He hated to wash himself with wine."
"268","(268) Yahya bin Saeed and Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, On the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Aisha saw Abd al-Rahman performing ablution, so she said: Perform ablution well, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Woe to the hocks from the Fire. (Ibn Majah 452. Ahmad 6/191)"
"269","(269) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw He greeted a people who performed ablution, but the water did not touch their heels, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Woe to the heels from the Fire.\n(Ahmad 3/316, Tabarani 781)"
"270","(270) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a people performing ablution with their heels waving, and he said: Woe to the heels of Fire, perform ablution properly. (Bukhari 60. Muslim 27)"
"271","(271) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he saw a people They perform ablution from the rain. He said: Perform ablution properly, for I heard Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Woe to the hocks of the Fire.\n(Bukhari 1650, Muslim 28)"
"272","(272) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Karib, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Woe to the hocks from the Fire. (Abu Dawud Tayalisi 1797. Ibn Majah 454)"
"273","(273) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of my father Imamah, or on the authority of his brother, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a people performing ablution, and he saw the butt of one of them emerging without the water hitting it, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Woe to the hocks from the Fire. (Ibn Majah 406. Tahawi 121)"
"274","(274) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Salma bin Qays, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: When you perform ablution, spread your hair, and if you perform ablution, perform Witr."
"275","(275) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit bin Sabrah, on the authority of His father, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about ablution? He said: Perform ablution thoroughly, and frequently inhale your nose, unless you are fasting."
"276","(276) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, who said: I heard Omar al-Anbari; He saw Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba performing ablution and forgot to blow his nose, so when the boy turned to him with the cup, he said: I forgot about the order of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he called for water and sniffed it twice."
"277","(277) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Satan has A bottle in which blows are blown, so when they stand up for prayer, their water is blown open, and at that they are ordered to scatter."
"278","(278) Waki’ and Ishaq al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Qaridh ibn Shayba, on the authority of Abu Ghatafan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Inhale two large mouthfuls, or three. Waki` said: Scatter yourself. (Abu Dawud 142. Ahmad 1/228)"
"279","(279) Abu Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They disliked the use of inhalation. Like snuff."
"280","(280) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu I saw that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever performs ablution, let him scatter, and whoever performs ablution, let him sprinkle water. (Muslim 212. Ahmad 2/236)"
"281","(281) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They used to rinse their mouths and sniff their mouths. And they scatter."
"282","(282) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Inhaling half of the bird."
"283","(283) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Inhalation is half the ritual purity."
"284","(284) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, that he saw Omar performing ablution and sprinkling his hair twice. Twice"
"285","(285) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They used to perform all the prayers with one ablution."
"286","(286) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: He had a ka’b to perform ablution. With it, then he performs all prayers with that ablution."
"287","(287) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Masoud bin Ali, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Sa’d said: If you perform ablution, pray With your ablution, that is what you did not do."
"288","(288) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yazid, the servant of Salama, on the authority of Salama; He used to perform the prayers with one ablution."
"289","(289) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Mujalid, who said: I saw Al-Sha’bi performing the prayers with one ablution."
"290","(290) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Zubayr ibn Adiyy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I pray the noon and afternoon prayers. Maghrib and Isha' are performed with the same ablution, unless I commit an action or say something reprehensible."
"291","(291) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man performs all the prayers with one ablution. It does not happen, and the same applies to tayammum."
"292","(292) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He used to sit and pray the noon prayer. Asr and Maghrib with one ablution."
"293","(293) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of a man called: Suleiman al-Basri, on the authority of the one who saw Omar. He prays the noon, afternoon and sunset prayers with one ablution."
"294","(294) Azhar al-Samman told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He would sometimes pray the noon prayer, then he would sit until He performs the Asr prayer, meaning with one ablution."
"295","(295) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: All prayers are performed with one ritual."
"296","(296) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: There is no ablution except from one who has performed it."
"297","(297) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Ablution without an event. Assault"
"298","(298) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I said to Shurayh: Should I perform ablution for every prayer? He said: Look what people do."
"299","(299) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman; He prayed the noon and afternoon prayers, and I do not know him except that he said: He prayed the Maghrib prayer, and he did not touch water."
"300","(300) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, that he said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution for every prayer, so when it was the day of the conquest, he performed all the prayers with ablution One\n(Abu Dawud 174. Ahmad 5/350)"
"301","(301) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: No. Ablution was performed unless it was broken."
"302","(302) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, that Ibn al-Aswad came to him from Medina while he was ill, so he prayed. Isha, while he was carrying one of his legs, and Fajr with one ablution."
"303","(303) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Masoud bin Ali, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Saad said: If you perform ablution, pray With your ablution as long as you do not perform it, and Ali said: When you stand up for prayer, wash your faces and your hands."
"304","(304) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The caliphs used to perform ablution for every prayer."
"305","(305) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: It was Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman, according to what Abu Khaled knows, perform ablution for every prayer, so when they are in the mosque, they supplicate. With the bowl."
"306","(306) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to hate the donkey's horn."
"307","(307) Abdul Rahman bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, and Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to hate the meat of a donkey and a dog."
"308","(308) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They both hated the meat of a donkey and a dog."
"309","(309) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to break the back of a mule. And the donkey."
"310","(310) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The mule is from the donkey."
"311","(311) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Hasan, that he used to hate the burden of a donkey, a mule, and a dog."
"312","(312) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He used to say: Do not perform ablution. With the meat of a donkey, or with the meat of a mule, or with the meat of any wild animal."
"313","(313) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ar, on the authority of Ibn Hakim, who said: I asked Abu Wa’il about the dog’s fasting? He said: I do not like to share it with you."
"314","(314) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see any harm in eating a donkey."
"315","(315) Muhammad bin Sawai told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Hubab; Jabir bin Zayd did not see any harm in killing a donkey."
"316","(316) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: There is no harm in the price of a donkey."
"317","(317) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked the arbiter, I said: Did I perform ablution thanks to the donkey’s veil and prayed? He said: Do not repeat it. And I asked Hammad? He said: I would love for you to repeat it."
"318","(318) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm in the price of a mule."
"319","(319) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm in the foot of every animal."
"320","(320) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the sacrifice of a horse, a camel, a cow, or a sheep."
"321","(321) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, and Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He saw no harm in riding a horse."
"322","(322) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They saw no harm in riding a horse."
"323","(323) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Every animal is eaten. Her flesh, there is no harm in performing ablution from her neck."
"324","(324) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the sacrifice of camels and cows. And the Shah"
"325","(325) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say that chickens drink from The vessel: it is disliked to perform ablution with it."
"326","(326) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, who said: Abu Qatada used to approach the felines. So he rinses on it, performs ablution with his veil and says: It is only a part of the household’s belongings."
"327","(327) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi informed me. Talha Al-Ansari, on the authority of Hamidah ibn Ubaid ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Kabsha bint Ka’b, who was the wife of some of the sons of Abi Qatada She poured water for Abu Qatada with which he could perform ablution, and then a cat came to drink, so the vessel listened to her, so I looked! He said: O my nephew, do you marvel? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not impure. It is from those who go around you, or: from the circumambulations. (Ahmad 5/309, Ibn Majah 367)"
"328","(328) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibn Hakim, who said: I asked Abu Wa’il about the feline’s surah? He said: There is no harm in it."
"329","(329) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Safiyya bint Dab, who said: I asked Al-Hussein bin Ali about the cat? He said: He is from Ahl al-Bayt."
"330","(330) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A cat is one of the household’s belongings."
"331","(331) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of a man from the people of Medina, who said: A bird was placed for Abdullah bin Omar, The feline drank from it, so Abdullah came to perform ablution from it, and he was told: The feline drank from it, so he said: It is from Ahl al-Bayt."
"332","(332) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the sound of felines."
"333","(333) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman al-Adani, who said: I heard Muhammad bin Ali saying: There is no harm in He performs ablution with the help of a cat, and says: It is one of the household’s belongings."
"334","(334) Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi told us, on the authority of al-Jaririyi, or Khalid, who said: A prostitute licked in a vessel by Abu al-Ala’. So he performed ablution thanks to her."
"335","(335) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in the slaughter of cats."
"336","(336) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib used to put He performs ablution, but something distracts him, so the cat comes and drinks from it, then he performs ablution from it and prays."
"337","(337) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: I heard Abu Imamah say: A cat is a possession. The house."
"338","(338) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Muslim Abu Ad-Dahhak al-Hamdani narrated to me, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of her master. Awf bin Malik Al-Jabri, on the authority of Ali; He was asked about the cat’s prayer? He said: There is no harm in it."
"339","(339) Waki’ told us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah and Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of his wife, Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of Abi Qatada, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The kitten is one of those who come around you. Or: from the tawaafat."
"340","(340) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: A kitten vomited milk for the Al-Alqamiya family, so they wanted To bury him, and Alqamah said: It is disgusting in my heart to bury him!"
"341","(341) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He said regarding the feline if it licks in the vessel, he said: It should be washed seven times. (Dar Qatni 67)"
"342","(342) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; In the vessel in which the cat licks, he said: He washes himself bitterly."
"343","(343) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a vessel that felines gnaw on? He said: He should be washed once."
"344","(344) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali, who said: I heard Ata’ say about a cat licking a vessel: He washes it seven times. Many times"
"345","(345) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The kitten is seven. (Dar Qatni 5. Ahmad 2/327)"
"346","(346) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: He should be washed twice."
"347","(347) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: It should be washed twice, or three times."
"348","(348) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Habib ibn Shihab, on the authority of his father, that he asked Abu Hurairah about the Surah of Taur. Is the woman purified from it? He said: If we were to jump around our bowl, we would both take a bath from it."
"349","(349) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not see anything wrong with a woman’s desire, unless she was menstruating, or in a state of sexual impurity."
"350","(350) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Madini, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a woman’s veil. ? He said: It has the softest skin and the sweetest scent."
"351","(351) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: There is no harm in the favor of a woman. She was not menstruating, or was junub."
"352","(352) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the virtue of a woman’s ablution."
"353","(353) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: There is no harm in performing the ablution of a woman."
"354","(354) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, that he was asked about the virtue of a menstruating woman performing ablution. From him? He said: Yes."
"355","(355) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a bath. May God bless him and grant him peace in his eyelids, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to wash with it, or to perform ablution. She said: O Messenger of God, I was junub, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Water does not junub. \n(Abu Dawud 69. Tirmidhi 65)"
"356","(356) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, who said: Abu Hajib narrated to us, on the authority of a man from Banu Ghaffar from The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a man to perform ablution because of The purity of the woman (Tirmidhi 63 Ahmad 5/66)"
"357","(357) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Sawada bin Asim, who said: You came to the Ghifari rule. And he is in the grave, and he forbade them about the virtue of a woman’s purification, so I said: Would it not be better if her arms were yellowed? Wouldn't he like such and such! So he took something and threw it away, saying: For you and your companions."
"358","(358) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Muhajir Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Kulthum bin Amir; Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith performed ablution, and I wanted to perform ablution thanks to her ablution, so she stopped."
"359","(359) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, and al-Hasan; They both hated the surplus of her purity."
"360","(360) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was forbidden for a man to perform ablution with the help of a woman’s ablution."
"361","(361) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, who said: I was with a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. I wanted to perform ablution with some of the water he had, but he said: Do not perform ablution with it, for it is a woman’s surplus."
"362","(362) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ghunaim ibn Qays, who said: If a woman is alone in performing ablution without you, then do not Perform ablution by its grace."
"363","(363) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, that the wife of Yazid bin Al-Shakhir drank and... She was menstruating, so Yazid performed ablution with it."
"364","(364) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Dhayyal, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I asked him about a man who performs ablution thanks to Menstruation drink? He saw no harm in it."
"365","(365) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, that he was asked about a menstruating woman drinking water, Should he perform ablution with it? He said: Yes, there is no problem with it."
"366","(366) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, who said: Omar said: She did not menstruate during her period. There it is."
"367","(367) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, on the authority of Abraham, that he saw no harm in a menstruating woman performing ablution. And it is disliked for her to drink."
"368","(368) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: There is no harm in the marriage of a menstruating woman, a woman in a state of sexual impurity, or a polytheist."
"369","(369) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and al-Hasan; Because they did not see any harm in her drinking, meaning the woman."
"370","(370) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maimunah, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I used to wash from one vessel. (Ahmad 329. Ibn Majah 377)"
"371","(371) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And he used to bathe from the bowl, while he and I were washing from the same vessel. (Bukhari 6/7339. Abu Dawud 242)"
"372","(372) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I wash from one vessel, and we are standing side by side. (Ahmed 1911, Abu Dawud 78)"
"373","(373) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama ibn Zaid, on the authority of al-Nu`man ibn Kharbudh, who said, I heard the mother of your young sons, the jiniya. It says: Perhaps the hands and hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, differed regarding performing ablution from a single vessel. (Abu Dawud 79. Ibn Majah 382)"
"374","(374) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, On the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama; She and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wash themselves from one vessel.\n(Bukhari 1929. Muslim 257)"
"375","(375) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I was taking a bath. And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from one vessel, we put our hands together."
"376","(376) Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salih, on the authority of Hamid bin Nafi’, on the authority of Umm Saad, the wife of Zayd bin Thabit She said: Zayd and I were taking a bath from one vessel of ritual impurity."
"377","(377) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: There is no harm in letting one’s body dry. From one vessel."
"378","(378) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj’s mother Al-Jadliyya, she said: Perhaps I disputed with Abd. God is the ablution."
"379","(379) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Shihab, on the authority of his father, that he asked Abu Hurairah? He said: If we are to jump \nAround our bowl, we both take a bath from it."
"380","(380) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A woman should bathe with her husband’s garment. And they extract from one vessel."
"381","(381) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: He was the Messenger of Allah May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he and his family wash from one vessel. (Ahmad 1/77 Ibn Majah 375)"
"382","(382) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ammar, who said: When a man and a woman take a bath from One vessel, the man began."
"383","(383) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, who said: A man and his wife should bathe. From one vessel."
"384","(384) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abd God, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his wives used to bathe from a single vessel. (Ibn Majah 379)"
"385","(385) Hushaym told us, he said: Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I was taking a bath. And the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was made from one vessel, but he was starting with it. (Ahmad 6/1700, Ibn Hibban 1193)"
"386","(386) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyyah, on the authority of Abu Sahil, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He forbade a woman and a man to wash from the same vessel."
"387","(387) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I do not make it permissible. For a person who performs ablution, he performs ablution in the mosque, and for the drinker and the one who performs ablution, it is permissible and a calamity."
"388","(388) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Mawhib, on the authority of Salih bin Muslim Al-Laythi, He said: I saw Ibn Jubayr bin Mutim in the mosque, checking for pebbles, then performing his complete ablution in the mosque."
"389","(389) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, who said: I saw Ibn Umar performing ablution in the mosque after he had urinated."
"390","(390) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I asked Abraham, but he did not see any harm in him."
"391","(391) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’? He said: We will perform ablution in the most sacred of them. The Grand Mosque."
"392","(392) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Majliz Aamah would not talk to us about the Qur’an, so perhaps The time for prayer came and he performed ablution in the mosque. He was told: An ablution to pass through? He said: Yes."
"393","(393) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in wiping ablution as long as one does not wash it. The man's relief"
"394","(394) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, who said: I saw a bird and a peacock performing ablution in the Sacred Mosque."
"395","(395) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, who said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I remembered for you that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution in the mosque."
"396","(396) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Husayn al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he disliked to sit in The mosque is being performed."
"397","(397) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I saw Uthman pouring water on him from a jug."
"398","(398) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Shaybani, on the authority of al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I saw a person performing ablution in a basin."
"399","(399) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin performing ablution in a toilet."
"400","(400) Yahya bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata’ about performing ablution in copper? He said: There is no harm in it. I said: The people hate it! He said: They hate its scent."
"401","(401) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Sila’, on the authority of Abd Khair, who said: We were with Ali. One day he prayed the lunch prayer, and when he left, he called the boy for the basin and performed ablution, then he put his fingers in his ears, then he said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution."
"402","(402) Ahmad bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salama, he said: Amr bin Yahya told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. So We brought out for him water in a bowl of water, and he performed ablution with it."
"403","(403) Yahya bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Muawiyah said: I was forbidden to perform ablution in copper."
"404","(404) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he did not drink from a cup of Zero, and one should not perform ablution with it. (Abdul Razzaq 180)"
"405","(405) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muslim Abi Farwa, who said: I saw Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla. He performs ablution in a basin in the mosque."
"406","(406) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to hate the yellow one. And he did not perform ablution in it."
"407","(407) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Jamil bin Zaid, who said: I saw Ibn Umar rinsing his mouth and sniffing from one palm."
"408","(408) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Ali, who said: He performed ablution, rinsed his mouth three times, and sniffed. Three, from one palm, and he said: This is the ablution of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"409","(409) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed ablution, took several scoops, rinsed his mouth and sniffed some of it."
"410","(410) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Rashid bin Ma’abad, who said: I saw Anas bin Malik rinsing his mouth and sniffing water. One palm"
"411","(411) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He used to gargle and sniffle with one water, Every time"
"412","(412) It was narrated on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymimi. He used to rinse his mouth and nose from one palm."
"413","(413) Khalid bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Jafar bin Maimun; He used to rinse his mouth and nose from one palm."
"414","(414) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad, that he used to rinse his mouth and sniff water, bitterly."
"415","(415) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He performs ablution when worms emerge from his anus."
"416","(416) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He does not have to perform ablution."
"417","(417) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a worm or worm emerges from the anus of a person, he will do so. Ablution"
"418","(418) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Abu al-Aliyah, who said: Whatever comes out of the upper half is not on him. There is ablution in it, and whatever emerges from the lower half must be ablution."
"419","(419) Abu Qutaybah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He performs ablution."
"420","(420) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Zayd, he said: I asked Ibrahim, I said: : It comes out of the anus of worms. Should I perform ablution with it? He said: No."
"421","(421) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Hind, he said: Ali said: I don’t care if I completed my ablution with whichever of my parts I started."
"422","(422) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Khalid, on the authority of Ziyad, who said: Ali said: I do not care if you start to the north before The right hand, if you perform ablution."
"423","(423) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Abdullah said: There is no harm in Start with your feet before your hands in ablution."
"424","(424) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Muja’ ibn Attab, on the authority of his father, he said: I performed ablution on Ali. He moved his ring."
"425","(425) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of a man, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali like him."
"426","(426) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Ibn Lahiya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hubayra, on the authority of Abu Tamim. Al-Jishani, that when Abdullah bin Amr performed ablution, he would move his ring, and that Abu Tamim used to do that, and that Ibn Hubayra used to do it."
"427","(427) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that when he performed ablution, he would move his ring."
"428","(428) Hussein bin Ali and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Marzuq, on the authority of Maymun; He used to move his ring when he performed ablution."
"429","(429) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim performing ablution with his ring in his hand, no He moves it."
"430","(430) Muhammad bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Omar, that Amr bin Dinar used to move his ring during ablution."
"431","(431) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: I heard Hammad saying regarding the Khatam: Remove it."
"432","(432) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Ishaq, a servant of Omar: that when Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz performed ablution He moved his ring."
"433","(433) Hanzala bin Thalan told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Al-Hasan performing ablution and moving his ring."
"434","(434) Ubaid al-Saydalani told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that he used to move his ring when He performed ablution."
"435","(435) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam, who said: There is ablution in regurgitation."
"436","(436) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: I asked him about regurgitation? He said: That is the da’sa, when it appears, it includes ablution."
"437","(437) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: There is ablution in regurgitation."
"438","(438) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you find food on your tongue, repeat the ablution."
"439","(439) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was a hadith."
"440","(440) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is ablution in regurgitation."
"441","(441) Abu Khaled told us, not in Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim and Salem. They said: There is ablution in regurgitation."
"442","(442) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, Mujahid, and Al-Hasan that they did not see ablution in qalql."
"443","(443) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, who said: Mujahid and Tawoos said: No, not until it results in vomiting."
"444","(444) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say regarding regurgitation: If it is easy, then it is not With something"
"445","(445) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hammad: Concerning regurgitation, if it is slight, then there is no ablution in it, and if it is A lot of times, including ablution."
"446","(446) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no ablution in reflux."
"447","(447) Hushaym, Ibn Aliyah, and Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd al-Adawi, who said: Al-Ala bin Ziyad narrated to us. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took a bath from his side and came out and saw a glint on his shoulder that had not been touched by water. So he took a bunch of it and wet it with it. (Dar Qatni 10)"
"448","(448) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man who left He presented him to a place of victory, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Perfect your ablution.” He said: Yunus: And he was the best. He says: That place should be washed."
"449","(449) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, that Omar bin al-Khattab saw A man had a shine on his foot that had not been poured with water while it was cleansed, so Omar said to him: With this ablution do you attend prayer?! And he commanded him to wash the mother and repeat the prayer."
"450","(450) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabab: that Omar saw a man praying, who had left his back. His feet were like nails, so he ordered him to repeat his ablution and prayer."
"451","(451) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Nakha’i, who said: Whatever water struck in places of birds, it He was pure"
"452","(452) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: I heard Ali ibn Husayn saying: The water did not hit From you, while you were beside yourself, that place was purified."
"453","(453) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim bin Abdullah performing ablution one day, and he left. There was a little something on his elbow, so he was told about that and he washed that place."
"454","(454) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus; Concerning a man who takes a bath and some part of him remains. He said: Then the water touches him, or he washes him."
"455","(455) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"456","(456) Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Hafsiya, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: He washes That place"
"457","(457) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir: that Omar saw on the foot of a man a place like a The penny did not get water on him, so he ordered him to repeat the ablution and repeat the prayer."
"458","(458) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He washes that place."
"459","(459) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muslim bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Abu Ali Al-Rahbi, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took a bath from his ritual impurity, and he saw a shine that had not been touched by water, so he said: He made it wet with it. (Ahmad 1/243 Ibn Majah 663)"
"460","(460) Asbat told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: That place should be washed."
"461","(461) Hushaym told us, saying: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he disliked performing ablution with water. The genitals"
"462","(462) Hushaym told us, saying: Abbad bin Misra told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He saw no harm in performing ablution. With fresh water."
"463","(463) Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Amr, and he said: I heard Al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymira that he hated to perform ablution. With fresh water."
"464","(464) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Ibrahim, who said: His followers were asked about the water that might come out: Should we perform ablution with it? He said: There is no harm in the water of the roads, and the water of the ringing. He said the roads: the one that animals trample and wade through, and the ringing water that I may go away."
"465","(465) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abu Al-Rabi’, who said: I was with Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, and he passed by With water in which animals wade and urinate, and he said: There is no harm in performing ablution from it."
"466","(466) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Easy water is more beloved to me than tayammum."
"467","(467) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Marzuq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A little Water is more beloved to me than dirt."
"468","(468) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Performing ablution using water is more beloved to me than tayammum."
"469","(469) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He was asked about the little water that does not Will he attain purity? He said: Upper Egypt is more beloved to me than that."
"470","(470) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Lahia, who said: I heard Ata’ saying: If you perform ablution and do not perform tayammum, then perform tayammum."
"471","(471) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah informed us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: that when he had a cup, he would wash his traces. Controversy"
"472","(472) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He and the black man were not to be bathed in water. Cupping"
"473","(473) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He used to wash the marks of the aspirants."
"474","(474) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they used to say: Wash the marks of the cuppers."
"475","(475) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, he said: They used to say; Concerning a man who has cupping: he performs ablution and washes the traces of cupping."
"476","(476) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul: He did not see any harm if he had a cup of hair, not to wash himself, or to He washes the traces of his chambers unless there is blood on them."
"477","(477) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan: He was asked about a man who uses cupping, what is wrong with him? He said: He washes the traces of his cups."
"478","(478) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Umar, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, who said: He washes the marks of the aspirants."
"479","(479) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim, Al-Qasim, Amir, and Tawus; I said: Should I take a bath after cupping? They said: No, Abu Ja`far said: Wash the traces of the cups."
"480","(480) Qabisa narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: He used to perform cupping and wash the marks of the cuppers. Then he performs his ablution for prayer, and prays."
"481","(481) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Mujbar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Qasim; Al-Qasim used to wipe the traces of the chambers with water."
"482","(482) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ghusl is a form of cupping."
"483","(483) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: Take a bath after cupping."
"484","(484) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Abraham and Mujahid had cupping in the presence of Abraham, so Mujahid took a bath. And Abraham washed the place of the chambers."
"485","(485) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man who uses cupping, or shaves his pubic hair, or plucks his armpits, he said: He takes a bath."
"486","(486) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Shayba, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr; Aisha told him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He takes a bath after cupping.\n(Abu Dawud 352, Ibn Khuzaymah 256)"
"487","(487) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: If a man has cupping, he should take a bath, but he did not consider it obligatory. (Abu Dawud 181, Tirmidhi 86)"
"488","(488) Waki’ ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He kissed some of his wives, then went out to pray, but did not perform ablution, so I said: Who is he but you? She laughed."
"489","(489) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. And Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He did not consider performing ablution in the qiblah."
"490","(490) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not consider performing ablution in the qiblah."
"491","(491) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no ablution in the qiblah."
"492","(492) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muslim bin Hayyan, On the authority of Masruq, he said: I don’t care whether I kiss her, or whether I kiss his hand."
"493","(493) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ruq, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed and then prayed, but he did not perform ablution. (Ahmad 210. An-Nasa’i 155)"
"494","(494) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no ablution in the qiblah."
"495","(495) Abd Allah bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He used to see the qibla from touching, and he would command her to perform ablution from it."
"496","(496) Hafs and Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: Abdullah said: The kiss is from touch, and this includes ablution."
"497","(497) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he kisses for desire, the ablution is invalidated."
"498","(498) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, similar to this."
"499","(499) Hushaym and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, the same."
"500","(500) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah, who said: I asked Al-Zuhari about the qiblah? He said: The scholars used to say: This includes ablution."
"501","(501) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: If he kisses or touches, then he must perform ablution."
"502","(502) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Kiss invalidates ablution."
"503","(503) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If a man kisses his wife and she does not want that, then it is It is obligatory to perform ablution on him, but no ablution is required of her. If she kisses him, then it is only obligatory to perform ablution on her, and it is not necessary to perform ablution on her. It is obligatory for him. If he finds something wrong, then it is obligatory for him to perform ablution, but if he kisses her while she does not want to do that, and she finds Yes, it is obligatory for her to perform ablution."
"504","(504) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said to his wife: As for me, I praise God, O Hanida. If I had not performed ablution, I would have kissed you."
"505","(505) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He kissed a boy and he rinsed his mouth."
"506","(506) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’; That Ibn Umar performed ablution and kissed his sons, so he called for water and rinsed his mouth."
"507","(507) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When a boy kissed him, he rinsed his mouth and did not perform ablution."
"508","(508) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about kissing a child after ablution? He said: It is only That is a mercy, there is no ablution in it."
"509","(509) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he touches or kisses for something, he breaks it. Ablution"
"510","(510) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Zechariah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, something similar."
"511","(511) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you kiss, or touch, or I began to repeat my ablution."
"512","(512) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, who said: If he touches, then he must perform ablution."
"513","(513) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not consider touching with the hand ablution."
"514","(514) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Layla, He said: If a man touches his wife for some sexual desire, he must perform ablution, unless he has ejaculated."
"515","(515) Ibn Idris and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about performing ablution with camel meat? He said: Perform ablution from her. (Ahmad 4/303, Ibn Khuzaymah 32)"
"516","(516) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah; That Abu Musa slaughtered a camel and fed his companions, then they stood up and prayed without ritual purification, but he forbade them from doing so, and said: What I don't care if I walked in its feces and blood and did not perform ablution, or I ate from its flesh and did not perform ablution."
"517","(517) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Abi Thawr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: We were We perform ablution with camel meat, but we do not perform ablution with sheep meat. (Tabarani 1868)"
"518","(518) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Israel?? On the authority of Ash'ath bin Abi Ash-Sha'tha'i, on the authority of Ja'far bin Abi Thawr, on the authority of Jabir bin Samarra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, we perform ablution with camel meat, and we do not perform ablution with sheep meat. (Ibn Hibban 1125. Ahmad 5/102)"
"519","(519) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Qais, who said: I saw Ibn Umar eating the meat of camels and drinking milk. Camels, and he prayed but did not perform ablution."
"520","(520) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, Ata’, and Mujahid. Because they did not perform ablution with camel meat or their milk."
"521","(521) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Sabara al-Nakhi’i; Omar bin Al-Khattab ate the meat of a camel, then he stood up and prayed but did not perform ablution."
"522","(522) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hassan; That Ali ate the meat of a camel, then he prayed but did not perform ablution."
"523","(523) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nafa’i bin Muslim, who said: I saw Suwayd bin Ghafli eating the meat of a camel, then he prayed without performing ablution."
"524","(524) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not in the meat of camels, cows and sheep. Ablution"
"525","(525) Hushaym told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Mandir told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah. He said: I ate bread and meat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman, so they prayed but did not They perform ablution. (Tirmidhi 80)"
"526","(526) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ate. He handed over his shoulder, then wiped his hand with the wipe that was underneath it, then he stood up and prayed. (Abu Dawud 1911, Ibn Hibban 1162)"
"527","(527) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Wahb ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas ; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate a bone, or ate a rib, then prayed, but did not perform ablution.\n(Ahmad 1/227 Ibn Khuzaymah 39)"
"528","(528) Hushaym told us, he said: Jabir al-Ju’fi told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He went out and wanted to pray, so he passed by a pot of Tafour, so he took a piece of it, or a shoulder, and ate it, then He rinsed his mouth but did not perform ablution. (Tabarani 10741. Ahmad 241)"
"529","(529) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Aoun told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, he said: I heard Abu He saw that Marwan spoke, saying: He performed ablution from what the fire touched, so Marwan sent to Umm Salamah to ask her, and she said: The Messenger of God has forgotten. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he was on my shoulder, then he went out to pray, and he did not touch water.\n(Ahmad 6/306, An-Nasa’i 6656)"
"530","(530) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, or Hussein bin Ali, on the authority of Zainab, daughter of Umm Salamah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought a shoulder of a sheep and he ate from it. He prayed but did not He touches water.\n(Ibn Majah 491. An-Nasa’i 187)"
"531","(531) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, he said: Suwayd bin told me Al-Numan Al-Ansari; They went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Khaybar, and when they were among the young men, he prayed the afternoon prayer, then called He fed him, and he was not brought except a large stalk, so they ate and drank, then he called for water and rinsed his mouth, then he got up and led the Maghrib prayer with us. (Ibn Majah 492)"
"532","(532) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of Suwayd bin Al-Nu’man, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with something similar to it, and adding to it: “And We rinsed our mouths with it, and he did not touch water.” (Ahmad 3/462)"
"533","(533) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Bilal narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Abi Amr narrated to me, on the authority of Hunayn bin Abi Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abi Rafi’, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, eat a shoulder, then stand up to pray. He did not touch water. (Muslim 94. Ahmad 6/392)"
"534","(534) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ja’far bin Amr bin Umayya. Al-Dhamri, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, grabbed the shoulder of a sheep, then prayed, but did not perform ablution.\n(Ahmad 4/1391 Muslim 93)"
"535","(535) Affan told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Iyad told us, he said: Iyad told me, on the authority of Suwayd bin Sarhan, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Bin Shu'ba, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate food, then the prayer was performed, and he had performed ablution before that. So I brought him some water so that he could perform ablution, and he turned to me and said: Behind you, and if you did that, the people would do that after me. (Tabarani 1008)"
"536","(536) Hushaym told us, he said: Amr bin Dinar and Abu Al-Zubair told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: I ate He brought bread and meat with Abu Bakr, so he prayed but did not perform ablution."
"537","(537) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Alqamiya and Al-Aswad were with Abdullah And he was going to the mosque, and he received a handful of porridge while he was in the spacious room. He said: So he sat down and ate some of it, along with some morsels of it. And Al-Aswad, he said: Then he called for water, rinsed his mouth, and washed his hands from the immersion of meat, then he went in and prayed."
"538","(538) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Wahb ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Jabir; That Abu Bakr ate bread and meat, nothing more than that he rinsed his mouth and washed his hands, then prayed."
"539","(539) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ablution is from what comes out, And not from what he entered."
"540","(540) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I never saw Ibn Umar performing ablution with food. He would lick his three fingers, then wipe his hand with dirt, then stand up to pray."
"541","(541) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: I said to Jabala: Did you hear Ibn Umar saying, “I eat meat and drink milk?” Do I pray, or do I perform ablution? He said: Yes."
"542","(542) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Yahya ibn Wathhab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ablution is from what comes out, It is not from what entered, nor from what was given to you."
"543","(543) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Ablution is from what comes out, not from what enters."
"544","(544) Ghandar and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zurara, that he heard Muhammad ibn Amr Ibn Ubayy narrates, on the authority of Umm al-Tufayl, Ubayy’s wife; That my father used to eat porridge, rinse his mouth, and pray."
"545","(545) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Arouba informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil. , on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal, on the authority of Umm Hakim Ibn Al-Zubair; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon hyenas; So he fell asleep on her shoulder, then went out to pray, but did not perform ablution. (Ahmad 6/419. Tabarani 214)"
"546","(546) Marhum bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Abu Al-Sawwar Al-Adawi eating porridge and meat, then He got up and prayed but did not perform ablution."
"547","(547) Abdă bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: An evil food is food from which one performs ablution."
"548","(548) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah; He used to eat porridge, drink wine, and pray, but did not perform ablution."
"549","(549) Ismail Ibn Aliyya narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I came to Ubaydah, so he ordered something to be done. So it was slaughtered, so he called for bread, milk, and ghee, and we ate it. Then he got up and prayed, but did not perform ablution, so I thought that he was more beloved to me. To perform ablution, had it not been that he wanted to show me that there was nothing wrong with him."
"550","(550) Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikay and Ikrimah, On the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pass by a pot, and he would take some of the sweat and some of it would be poured out, then he would pray. He did not perform ablution, nor did he touch water. (Ahmad 6/161)"
"551","(551) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Khutmi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, who said: Abdullah bin Yazid eats meat and porridge, so he prays but does not perform ablution."
"552","(552) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I heard Uthman, the client of Thaqif, narrating, on the authority of Abu Ziyad, he said: I witnessed Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurairah were waiting for a kid of theirs in the oven. Ibn Abbas said: Bring it out for us. He gave us a test in prayer, so they took it out and ate from it. Then Abu Hurairah performed ablution, and Ibn Abbas said to him: We have eaten. An abomination?! He said: Abu Hurairah said: You are better than me and more knowledgeable. Then they prayed."
"553","(553) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah Ibn Qariz; Abu Hurairah ate the bulls of a cat, so he got up and performed ablution and said: Do you know why I performed ablution? I ate the remains of a cat. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Perform ablution from what the fire has touched. He said, and it was ‘Umar. He performs ablution after intoxication."
"554","(554) Ibn Numair narrated to us, he said: Othman bin Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Sufyan bin Al-Mughirah bin Al-Akhnas; He entered upon his maternal aunt, the mother of his beloved, and she made him drink something from a stalk, then said: O son of my sister, perform ablution. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Perform ablution from whatever the fire has touched."
"555","(555) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Abdul Aziz al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, He said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf told me, he said: Abu Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Akhnasi told me, he said: I entered On my maternal aunt, the mother of my beloved, who made me drink a waterthorn, then she said: O son of my sister, perform ablution, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, says: Perform ablution from whatever the fire has touched. (Ahmad 6/328)"
"556","(556) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: It was said to Matar al-Warraq, and I am with him: about the one who took al-Hasan, that he was Should he perform ablution after touching the fire? He said: He took it from Anas, Anas took it from Abu Talha, and Abu Talha took it from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Tahawi 69. Ahmad 4/30)"
"557","(557) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: Perform ablution from The fire touched."
"558","(558) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Kharijiyah ibn Zayd, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, that He said: Perform ablution from whatever the fire has touched. (Tabarani 4839)"
"559","(559) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; That Abu Musa was performing ablution from what was changed by the fire."
"560","(560) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, who said: I went to Anas bin Malik and did not find him, so I sat I was waiting for him, and he came and was angry, and said: I was with this man, meaning the pilgrims. They ate, then they got up and prayed, but he did not They perform ablution! So I said: Why were you doing this, O Abu Hamza? He said: What we used to do. (Abdul Razzaq 670)"
"561","(561) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He drank fresh water and performed ablution."
"562","(562) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, that Anas, Abu Talha, Abu Musa, Ibn Umar, and Zaid bin Thabit, and two women from the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; They used to perform ablution from what the fire had changed."
"563","(563) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab; He used to command people to perform ablution after the fire had changed, and he made them drink bitter wine, so he brought them ablution, so they performed ablution."
"564","(564) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, who said: Perform ablution from Sugar, for it has dregs."
"565","(565) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Aisha, Abu Salamah, and Omar bin Abdul Aziz; They used to perform ablution from what had touched the fire, and Al-Zuhri used to perform ablution from it."
"566","(566) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of a man of the tail, I see him mentioning that he has As a companion, he said: He should perform ablution from what fire has changed."
"567","(567) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Shayba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ibrahim, who said: I was with Abu Hurairah. So he performed ablution above the mosque, and I said to him: From what did you perform ablution? He said: I ate my bull in pluck."
"568","(568) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qur’a ibn Khalid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Perform ablution from what has been changed by fire."
"569","(569) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating, that he heard Abu Al-Shifar narrating, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Amr said: They were with Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, and they ate meat and porridge, and they left him and began to pray. They do not perform ablution, so Abu Masoud said: Look! They pray but do not perform ablution."
"570","(570) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Al-Aizar, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, he said: Umar ibn Al-Khattab saw a man He scratched his armpit, or touched it, and said to him: Get up and wash your hand, or purify yourself."
"571","(571) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar said: Whoever cleans his nose, or scratches his armpits He performed ablution."
"572","(572) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He does not have to perform ablution in plucking Armpit"
"573","(573) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man touching his armpits, or plucking them? He did not see any harm in it, unless he bloodied it."
"574","(574) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: These people say: Whoever touches his armpits repeats ablution? I do not say that, nor do I know what this is."
"575","(575) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; He used to take a bath by plucking his armpits."
"576","(576) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; What about a man who takes some of his hair and nails after he performs ablution? He said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"577","(577) Hushaym told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, about Al-Hakam and Ata’, they said: There is nothing wrong with him, he only added to it. Purely"
"578","(578) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: It is pure and blessed."
"579","(579) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hafs bin Abi Dawud, on the authority of Asim, who said: I saw Abu Wa’il cut some of his hair, Then he entered the mosque and prayed."
"580","(580) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, Ata’, Al-Hakam, and Al-Zuhri. They said: It is not upon him. Ablution"
"581","(581) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: I saw Ibn Umar taking some of his nails. So I said to him: Have you taken some of your nails, and are you not performing ablution? He said: What are your bags?! You are more wise than those whom his family called wise."
"582","(582) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man who takes some of his hair and nails. He said: He is performing ablution."
"583","(583) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Water is poured over him."
"584","(584) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He runs water over him."
"585","(585) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ali bin Muslim, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man taking some of his nails, he said: He is repeating ablution."
"586","(586) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Mus’ar, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: When he wrote He performed ablution on his nails."
"587","(587) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn Zur, on the authority of his father, who said: He performs ablution for that."
"588","(588) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man trimming his nails, and taking some of his beard, he said: wiping it with water."
"589","(589) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who cuts his nails, he said: He washes them with water."
"590","(590) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yasar bin Numayr, who said: Whenever Omar urinated, he wiped his penis against a wall. Or with a stone, and no water has touched it."
"591","(591) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, or Malik bin Al-Harith, who said: Sa’d passed by a man who was washing He was indifferent, so he said: Why do you mix in your religion something that is not part of it?!"
"592","(592) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mustarid, who said: Mujma’ ibn Yazid saw me while I was washing my penis. He said: Didn't you shake your hair when you urinated? I said: Yes, he said: It is enough for you."
"593","(593) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: My father would not wash his urinary tract, he would perform ablution. He does not touch water."
"594","(594) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’; Ibn al-Zubayr saw a man washing his penis, so he said: Should he not wash his penis?"
"595","(595) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who urinated and forgot to wash his penis, he said: That is sufficient for him."
"596","(596) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubaid Allah Ibn al-Qubtiyya, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr; He saw a man washing off a trace of excrement, so he said: What were we doing to him?"
"597","(597) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yahya al-Tawwam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went to urinate, and Omar followed him with a water supply, and he said: What is this, O Omar? He said: Water to perform ablution with, and he said: I was not commanded to perform ablution every time I urinate, and if I had done so it would have been Sunnah. (Abu Dawud 43, Ibn Rahwayh 1262)"
"598","(598) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Abdullah, the client of Banu Makhzum, who said: I saw Ibn Umar washing Traces of urine."
"599","(599) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I saw a man washing traces of urine, and I saw Ibn Sirin He washes the traces of urine, and I saw Al-Nadr ibn Anas washing the traces of urine."
"600","(600) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, Ibn Abbas said: Praise be to you for washing the urethra."
"601","(601) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of a man from Banu Asad, who said: I saw Abu Hurairah urinate, so he washed something. Here you are"
"602","(602) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He urinated, then took water, put his hand in his cloth, and wiped it. He mentioned it."
"603","(603) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that he urinated and then entered He put his hand in his trousers and washed his penis."
"604","(604) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: Whenever Abraham urinated, he put his hand under it. He removed his garment and wiped his penis, so I mentioned that to Talha and he liked it."
"605","(605) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, he said: I saw Ibrahim urinate and wash his penis."
"606","(606) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Omar, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Tawoos; Concerning a man who performed ablution and immersed his feet in the water, he said: This is useless."
"607","(607) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Ata’, Aamir, and Salim about a man performing ablution, and he did so. His feet in the water? They said: It is sufficient."
"608","(608) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he plunges his feet into the water, then that is sufficient for him. Ablution"
"609","(609) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He may have performed ablution on his armpits in the summer."
"610","(610) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated it"
"611","(611) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, who said: I entered a house with Abu Hurairah. Marwan called for ablution, and he performed ablution. When he washed his arms, he went beyond the elbows. When he washed his feet, he went beyond the ankles to the elbows. The legs, so I said: What is this? He said: This is the amount of the jewelry. (Bukhari 5953, Muslim 219)"
"612","(612) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub Al-Bajli, on the authority of Abu Zur’i, who said: I entered upon my father. So he performed ablution up to his shoulders and to his knees, so I said to him: Are you not satisfied with what God has made obligatory upon you? This? He said: Yes, but I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The amount of jewelry is the amount of ablution, so I loved To increase my sweetness. \n(Muslim 101)"
"613","(613) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who went out to Prayer and he had intercourse with a virgin? He said: If it is wet, it will wash away what came upon it, and if it is dry, it will not harm you."
"614","(614) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: Concerning a man who has intercourse with a virgin while he is pure. He said: If it is wet, he will wash away whatever came upon it, and if it is dry, then nothing is wrong. Aliyah"
"615","(615) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If it is wet, he should wash it, and if it is It is dry, so it will not harm it."
"616","(616) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Concerning a man who has intercourse with a wet virgin, he said: He washes it, but does not perform ablution."
"617","(617) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; So whoever has intercourse with a dead body, or a menstruating woman, or a withered virgin: there is no problem."
"618","(618) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Talha, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: There is no harm with a stomach. It is mixed with urine."
"619","(619) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Sinan bin Habib, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who had intercourse with a virgin while he was going to the mosque. He said: Abraham said: No, he should repeat ablution."
"620","(620) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amara, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of the mother of a son of Ibrahim bin Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, she said: I was extending my tail, passing by a dirty place and a good place, so I entered upon Umm So I asked her, and Umm Salama said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: He purifies what comes after him.\n(Tabarani 846. Malik 16)"
"621","(621) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Zaid, on the authority of a woman from his children. Abdul-Ashhal, she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Is there a dirty road between it and the mosque? He said: Is there a cleaner path after it? She said: Yes, he said: This is it. (Ahmad 6/435)"
"622","(622) Hushaym told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of the one who told him on the authority of Aisha; She was asked about a man who passes by a dirty place while in his state of ritual ablution? She said: He may pass by a clean place and purify one another."
"623","(623) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The earth is purified one by another."
"624","(624) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: It has informed me on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Ibn Abbas that: They used to say: The earth purifies one another."
"625","(625) Sharik, Hushaym, and Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: We were not We perform ablution from a place of rest. (Abu Dawud 206)"
"626","(626) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: The earth purifies one another."
"627","(627) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamiya and al-Aswad; Indeed, they did not perform ablution for what they had intercourse with."
"628","(628) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: No ablution from a place of footing."
"629","(629) Al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: He who pays zakat on the land wears it."
"630","(630) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of al-Harith bin Umair, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalababi, he said: If it dries The earth has become pure."
"631","(631) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail Al-Azraq, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, who said: If the land dries up, it becomes good."
"632","(632) Marhum bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Al-Hasan sitting with traces of dried urine, so I asked him? He said: It is dry."
"633","(633) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah It is mentioned on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: rinse your mouth with milk, for it has a fat content."
"634","(634) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example. (Ahmad 1/329)"
"635","(635) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Yaqoub Al-Zam’i, who said: Ibn Abi Ubaidah bin Abdullah informed me Ibn Zam`a, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: When you drink milk and rinse your mouth with some of it, it has a fat content."
"636","(636) Ibn Uyaynah and Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin; Anas bin Malik and Al-Harith Al-Hamdani used to rinse their mouths with milk three times."
"637","(637) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Khutmi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid said: He used to drink milk and rinse his mouth."
"638","(638) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of a man of Dhail. I see him mentioning that he has My companions said: One should rinse the mouth with milk, but not with dates."
"639","(639) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever eats meat or drinks milk, let him rinse his mouth, if I wish"
"640","(640) Abdou told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was commanded to rinse the mouth with milk."
"641","(641) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan; That Abu Musa, Anas, and Al-Harith Al-Hamdani used to rinse their mouths with milk."
"642","(642) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu Saeed said: There is no ablution except with milk, because it comes out from between feces and blood."
"643","(643) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Othman bin Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah He says: There is no ablution except with milk."
"644","(644) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Al-Qasim about rinsing the mouth, or performing ablution using milk? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"645","(645) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yazid Al-Shaybani narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd al-Malik bin Misra, on the authority of Ibn Wathiyl; Hudhaifa called for milk and he drank and I drank, then he called for water and he rinsed his mouth and I rinsed my mouth."
"646","(646) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that Ibn Abbas drank milk, so they mentioned it to him. Ablution and rinsing the mouth. He said: I don’t care, allow it, and it will be allowed for you."
"647","(647) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qur’a ibn Khalid, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of his brother Mutarrif ibn al-Shakhir, who said: I drank milk. Just after I performed ablution, I asked Ibn Abbas, and he said: I don’t care at all. Allow it, and it will be permitted for you."
"648","(648) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Talha, who said: I asked Abu Abdul Rahman about performing ablution with milk. He said: From a drink that is pleasant to the drinkers."
"649","(649) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: I said to Jabaliya: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I eat meat and drink milk. Do I pray or do ablution? He said: Yes."
"650","(650) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: Abu Abdul Rahman was in the mosque, so he came to it. Mudrik bin Amara had milk and drank it. Mudrik said: This is water, so he rinsed his mouth. He said: From what? The security of the good jeweler?!"
"651","(651) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Jabr bin Atik, who said: Ibn Omar was in our house, so we brought him an ablution made of brass, and he disapproved of it and said: Bring me a stone or wood."
"652","(652) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Umm Ghurab, on the authority of Banana, that Uthman used to perform ablution in a jug or a barrel made of barrels."
"653","(653) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to perform ablution in a human being, or in a wooden bowl."
"654","(654) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Marzuq Abi Bukair, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: A man asked Ibn Abbas, he said: We are looking for pasture and cannot find water, so we should perform ablution with milk? He said: No, you have to perform tayammum."
"655","(655) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of someone who heard Al-Hasan say: He should not perform ablution with wine or milk."
"656","(656) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abraham: Concerning a fly that falls into a vessel and dies. He said: There is no harm in it."
"657","(657) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, that he did not see harm in the scorpion. And the beetles and every soul that is not a beggar."
"658","(658) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’: They saw no harm in the beetle or the scorpion. And the insistence."
"659","(659) Waki’ narrated to us, Abdullah bin Sabrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a chicken that died in a well, he said: The prayer should be repeated from it and the clothes should be washed."
"660","(660) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: Recite to me a verse about washing clothes."
"661","(661) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan saying: If you are certain that you performed ablution while in the well, then trust is in Washing clothes and repeating prayer."
"662","(662) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And if he wanted to sleep while he was junub, he would perform his ablution for prayer. (Muslim 248 Ibn Majah 584)"
"663","(663) Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Aisha; If the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to sleep, he would perform ablution, and if he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands. It means, while he is beside himself. (Ibn Majah 593. Abu Dawud 225)"
"664","(664) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, who said: Ali said: If a man becomes junub and wants to He eats, or sleeps, performing ablution for prayer."
"665","(665) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; If he wanted to eat or sleep while in state, he would wash his face and hands, and wipe his head."
"666","(666) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: If one of you wants to lie down and Side?? Let him perform ablution, for he does not know whether he will be afflicted in his dream."
"667","(667) Ibn Mubarak and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha; He was asked: Should we eat junk food? He said: Yes, and he walked in the markets."
"668","(668) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, who said: Then If one of you is in a state of ritual impurity during the night, then he wants to sleep, let him perform ablution, for that is half of the state of ritual impurity."
"669","(669) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, who said: If a junub person wants to eat, Or he sleeps, let him perform his ablution for prayer."
"670","(670) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, and Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said : If a junub person wants to eat, he washes his hands and rinses his mouth."
"671","(671) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Mujahid; He eats during the state of sexual impurity? He said: He washes his hands and eats."
"672","(672) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: If he wants to be in a state of junubah, he may sleep before he He performs ablution."
"673","(673) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a person in a state of impurity wants to eat, he washes himself. His hands"
"674","(674) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A person who is in a state of ritual impurity drinks water before he performs ablution."
"675","(675) Ibn Aliyah, Ghandar, and Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a state of impurity, he wanted to eat or sleep. He performs ablution.\n(Muslim 248. Abu Dawud 226)"
"676","(676) Ruh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Adniy, who said, I heard Muhammad ibn Ali saying regarding sexual impurity. If he wants to sleep, eat, or drink: he performs ablution as he does for prayer."
"677","(677) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, and Abu Qalab, who said: Omar of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, consulted a fatwa. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. How can one of us sleep while he is junub? He said: He performs ablution and sleeps. Ayyoub said, I think in the hadith of Abu Qalaba: washing the private parts.\n(Bukhari 290. Tahawi 127)"
"678","(678) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: narrated to us Abu Salamah; He asked Aisha: Did the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, lie while he was in a state of junub? She said: Yes, and his ablution is performed for prayer.\n(Bukhari 2864, Ahmad 6/128)"
"679","(679) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, On the authority of his father, he said: If a person in a state of ritual impurity wants to eat, sleep, or drink, he should perform ablution."
"680","(680) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a junub person wants to eat Or when he sleeps, he performs ablution."
"681","(681) Othham bin Ali told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; Concerning a man who is afflicted with a ritual impurity during the night and wants to sleep. She said: He should perform ablution or perform tayammum."
"682","(682) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Will impurity befall me and I should lie down? He said: If you want to lie down, perform ablution. (Bukhari 2898 Muslim 24)"
"683","(683) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He permitted the one in a state of impurity, if he wanted to sleep, eat, or drink, to perform the ablution required for prayer. (Abu Dawud 227 Tirmidhi 613)"
"684","(684) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Burd ibn Sinan, on the authority of Ubad ibn Nasi, on the authority of Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, he said: I came Aisha, so I said: Did you see that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was taking a bath on the first day of the night to remove ritual impurity, or during The last one? She said: Maybe he took a bath at the beginning of the night, and maybe he took a bath at the end of it. (Ahmad 6/138, Tirmidhi 2924)"
"685","(685) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Hudhayf, he said: Sleeping before washing is more difficult for him to go out."
"686","(686) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughul, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, who said: Hudhayfy said: Sleeping after ritual ritual impurity. I am tired of washing."
"687","(687) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was If he had a need, he would fulfill it for his family, then he would sleep as he was, without touching water. (Ibn Majah 582)"
"688","(688) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If a man has intercourse and then wants to go back There is no harm in delaying washing. (Tabarani 9213)"
"689","(689) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He told us on the authority of his maternal aunt. Maimunah, she said: I provided a bath for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he took a bath from the ritual impurity, so he placed the vessel with his left side. On his right hand, and he washed his hand, then he poured water on his private part and washed it, then he rubbed his hand on the ground, then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed. He washed his face and arms, then he sprinkled water on his head, then he sprinkled water on his entire body, then he stepped aside and washed his feet. She said: So I brought him a garment and he put it back on, and he started speaking like this with water. The water is shaken off. (Ahmad 335. Tirmidhi 103)"
"690","(690) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took a bath to remove ritual impurity. He began by washing his palms three times, then he performed his ablution. For prayer, then he inserted his hand and mixed it with the roots of the hair, until it seemed to me that he had cleared the skin, then poured water on his head. He poured water three times, then he poured water over his entire body. (Bukhari 248. An-Nasa’i 246)"
"691","(691) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told us, He said: Aisha told me; When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would wash himself after ritual impurity, a vessel would be placed for him and he would pour on his blood before To put them both into the vessel, so that when he washed his hands, he inserted his right hand into the vessel, then poured with the right hand and washed. He poured it with the left, and when he was finished, he poured the right on the left and washed it, then he rinsed his mouth and inhaled three times, then poured On his head, fill his hands three times, then wash the rest of his body. (Ahmad 6/173. An-Nasa’i 244)"
"692","(692) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Khalid, who said: When Omar was in a state of ritual impurity, he would wash himself. He removed it, then he performed his ablution for prayer, then he emptied it."
"693","(693) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning washing oneself from impurity, he said: He performs his ablution for prayer, then he washes off whatever came on him, then he strikes with his hand. He rubs it with dirt, then washes it, then pours water over it."
"694","(694) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I asked Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla about Washing from impurity? He said: You wash your palms, then rub your right hand over your left, then you wash your private parts, then you wash your hands, then Perform your ablution for prayer."
"695","(695) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi. He used to say in the state of ritual impurity: He would begin by washing his right hand, then he would wipe it over his left hand. He washes his private parts and any of his semen, then rubs his hand against the wall, then performs ablution."
"696","(696) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was said: Purification before washing."
"697","(697) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Regarding washing from impurity: If you wash your hands, start with the verse. You wish"
"698","(698) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He did not consider performing ablution in the ritual ablution for ritual impurity."
"699","(699) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, who said: A group of the people of Iraq went out to Omar and asked him about Washing one’s body? He said: You asked me about qualities that no one has asked me about since I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace! As for washing one’s ritual impurity, perform ablution as you do for prayer. (Saeed bin Mansour 2143)"
"700","(700) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Surad, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim, who said: They debated in Washing was done by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Some of the people said: As for me, I wash my head in such-and-such ways, so he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: As for me, I will cover my head with three palms. (Muslim 258. An-Nasa’i 247)"
"701","(701) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said A man asked him: How much should I pour water on my head while I am junub? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to scratch his head three times, and the man said: My hair is long. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was more poetic and kinder than you. (Ibn Majah 578)"
"702","(702) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, we are in a cold land. So how to wash oneself from impurity? He said: As for me, I will cover my head with water three times. (Bukhari 255. An-Nasa’i 233)"
"703","(703) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a bath after ritual impurity, and poured water on his head three times."
"704","(704) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Bukair ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of al-Ma’roor ibn Suwayd, who said: Omar said: As for me So I pour three times over my head."
"705","(705) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Yazid, who heard Ibn Abbas say: The impurity envelops oneself. His head is three."
"706","(706) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He scoops three times on his head."
"707","(707) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He used to wash his head twice for ritual impurity."
"708","(708) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, some people from the people of Taif said to him: Our land is cold, so what will suffice for us? Washing? He said: As for me, I will wrap my head in three handfuls."
"709","(709) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani’, she said: When she has washed herself from impurity, So wash every part of you three times."
"710","(710) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Marzuq, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, that a man asked him, and he said: Wash three times. He said: I have a lot of hair. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had more hair than you. And the best.\n(Ahmad 3/54, Ibn Majah 576)"
"711","(711) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Rayhani, on the authority of Sifina, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wash himself with a saa’ and purify himself with the mud. (Muslim 258 and Ibn Majah 267)"
"712","(712) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he washes himself with the sewage, and that is the mug. (Ibn Majah 3761 and Ibn Rahwayh 557)"
"713","(713) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: One mudd of ablution suffices, and one sa’ of ritual impurity suffices. Then a man said: It is not enough for us, O Jabir. He said: Someone who is better than you and has more poetry is sufficient."
"714","(714) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; That a man told them, saying: I entered upon Aisha, and I said: O Mother of the Believers, he did not make up for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: So she called for a vessel that I had prepared for a saa’ of this saa’ of yours."
"715","(715) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibn Jabr, on the authority of Anas, who said: You perform ablution with the mudd, and you bathe with up to five sa’’s. supplies (Bukhari 201)"
"716","(716) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: Jabir was asked about washing The impurity? He said: A saa’, and he said: I don’t think it is enough for me? Jabir said: Yes."
"717","(717) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, who heard Ibn Abbas say: A saa’ is sufficient. For the one who is in a state of impurity, and Ubayd Allah said: I do not know before or after ablution?"
"718","(718) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He performed ablution with a muddle of water, and bathed with a saa’."
"719","(719) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Safiyya Ibn Shaybib, on the authority of Aisha, In the same way"
"720","(720) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Atiyya, who said: I saw Ibn Umar performing ablution from a jug and pouring water into it. I said: Is it a tide? He said: And better."
"721","(721) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They used to see a mudd for ablution, and a saa’ for washing."
"722","(722) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: A man is sufficient For his ghusl, a quarter of a portion."
"723","(723) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yassaf, who said: It used to be said: Part of ablution is extravagance, even if I was on the shore of a river."
"724","(724) Qattan bin Abdullah Abu Marri told us, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: I saw Abu Imamam performing ablution with a jug of water."
"725","(725) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Simak, who said: I saw Jabir bin Samurah being brought with a cup. of water, so he performed ablution and wiped over his socks, then he prayed the afternoon prayer, while I was watching."
"726","(726) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Dinar, who said: I saw Salim performing a light ablution."
"727","(727) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, he said: I saw Amr ibn Murrah performing ablution and no water flowed, meaning: from his lack of water."
"728","(728) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: He had a ka’b to perform ablution. With this, Abu Muawiyah added: The value of a man’s opinion."
"729","(729) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, on the authority of Abu Al-Hudhail; He saw a neighbor of his performing ablution, so he said: Go for ablution."
"730","(730) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: The first thing that begins with obsessiveness is Ablution"
"731","(731) Yazeed told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of someone who told him on the authority of Abu Darda’, he said: Go for ablution, even if I was on the shore of a river."
"732","(732) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I do not perform ablution with a cup of love twice, meaning: For half a cup."
"733","(733) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say: Too much ablution is from Satan.\n(Ibn Khuzaymah 122. Tayalisi 547)"
"734","(734) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated to slap their faces. With water, they smeared it little by little."
"735","(735) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the two waters meet, then the ablution has been completed."
"736","(736) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Khalid bin Zayd, who said: I saw Ibn Umar performing ablution and he was sipping water. May his face be of age."
"737","(737) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: Abdullah said: Water after trace Water is sufficient, and there is nothing after the three."
"738","(738) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sawada bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He performed ablution with a cup."
"739","(739) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Hafs, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Al-Bayhi, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution with a cup."
"740","(740) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Ibn Jabr, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He performed ablution with two pounds of water. (Ahmad 3/1791 Abu Dawud 96)"
"741","(741) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prescribed inhalation. Three times in ritual impurity. (Dar Qatni 115)"
"742","(742) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Fudayl bin Amr, who said: Omar said: If you wash impurity, then rinse your mouth three times, for that is the most eloquent."
"743","(743) Abu Amer Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Abdullah bin Rahimah, he said: Your grandmother told me; When Othman took a bath from ritual impurity, he would rub his mouth with his finger three times."
"744","(744) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Aban Al-Attar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Hassan bin Bilal, who said: Inhaling urine is bitter. From defecation twice, and from impurity three times."
"745","(745) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, he said: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abd told me. The Most Gracious, he said: Aisha told me; When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a bath after ritual impurity, he would rinse his mouth and nose three times."
"746","(746) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his leaders, who said: He used to say: Rinse your mouth three times after impurity, and whoever To defecate twice, and to urinate once."
"747","(747) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to prefer it. To inhale the impurity three times."
"748","(748) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ghanim bin Qays, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He was asked about ablution after Washing? He said: What ablution is more comprehensive than washing?!"
"749","(749) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He does not perform ablution after washing from ritual impurity. (Ibn Majah 579. Ahmad 6/258)"
"750","(750) Abu Al-Ahwas Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: A man from the neighborhood said to Ibn Umar: I perform ablution after washing. He said: You have delved deeply into it."
"751","(751) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man came to Alqamiya and said to him: Your brother’s daughter performed ablution. After washing, he said: If she were with us, she would not do that, and any ablution is more comprehensive than washing."
"752","(752) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: There is no ablution more comprehensive than washing."
"753","(753) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Abi Habibi, Jabir bin Zayd was asked about a man who took a bath from The impurity, so he performed his ablution for prayer, then he left his bath. Should he perform ablution? He said: No, it is sufficient for him to wash his feet."
"754","(754) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muadh bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I asked him about ablution after washing from The impurity? His thoughts"
"755","(755) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Ikrimah; Concerning a man who performs ablution from ritual impurity, and you attend prayer. Should he perform ablution? He said: No."
"756","(756) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hudhayf, who said: Is it not sufficient? One of you should wash from the top of his horn to his feet, until he performs ablution!"
"757","(757) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was said: Purification before washing."
"758","(758) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: A man said to Abdullah: : So-and-so performed ablution after washing, and he said: If she had been with me, she would not have done that."
"759","(759) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Al-Bakhtari; That Ali was performing ablution after washing."
"760","(760) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maymunah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a bath, then stepped aside and washed his feet."
"761","(761) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Muslim ibn Yasar, on the authority of Hamran; When Othman took a bath of ritual impurity, he would come out of his bath and wash the soles of his feet. He said: And Muslim said: I don’t care if I come out of my ablution to my prayer place."
"762","(762) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, Muslim ibn Yassar said: I don’t care if I wash myself with water. The ritual impurity in a clean place, then I go out to my mosque."
"763","(763) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the place in which one takes bath is The janaba is soaked in water, so let him wash his feet when he has finished, and if they are clean, then he may wash them if he wishes."
"764","(764) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: A man asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: What do you think when you take a bath? Is washing from ritual impurity sufficient for me to perform ablution? He said: Yes, but wash your feet."
"765","(765) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: When you go out, wash your feet."
"766","(766) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Al-Hasan, or Mujahid: How do you do with your feet? Washing from impurity? He said: As for me, I say like this. Ibn Aoun described that he poured water on the backs of his feet."
"767","(767) Hushaym told us, saying: The common people told us, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi; He used to say in a state of ritual impurity when he had finished: “Let him wash his feet when he left his bath.”"
"768","(768) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muadh ibn al-Ala’, he said: We asked Sa’id ibn Jubayr, and he said: If he was in his place. He washed his feet, otherwise he did not."
"769","(769) Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you perform ablution in a bath, he will take care of it. So wash your feet when you go out."
"770","(770) Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Ashja’i, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about washing one’s body. The impurity? He said: Spread water on yourself, then step aside and wash your feet."
"771","(771) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of al-Mustamir ibn al-Rayyan, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza’i, who said: If a man takes a bath in The one who has bathed and is clean does not wash his feet, and if he is not clean then he washes his feet."
"772","(772) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in separating his ritual ghusl from impurity."
"773","(773) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in a person in a state of impurity washing his head before his body, or his body before his head."
"774","(774) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala; A man from his family had taken a bath from ritual impurity and had forgotten to wash his head. He said: So he ordered me to ask Saeed bin Al-Musayyab. About that, I asked him, and he said: Let him come back and wash his head. He said: So I went and poured some water on him from his ablution until he washed his head. His head"
"775","(775) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Salama bin Abd al-Rahman used to conceal His family, and he hated that they should know about him, and he used to wash his body up to his throat, and he hated that they should wash his head. So they learned about it, so his family came and said: I have pain in my head, so he called for the marshmallow and he washed it."
"776","(776) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Al-Azma’, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever washes his head With marshmallow while he is junub, so he has completed the ritual ablution."
"777","(777) Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, the same."
"778","(778) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whoever washes his head while he is junub He has completed the ritual ablution."
"779","(779) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of al-Harith ibn al-Azma’, he said: I heard Abdullah says: Whoever washes his head with marshmallow while he is in a state of ritual impurity, has performed the ritual ablution. Al-Harith said: But he should not return the marshmallows that spilled on his head either. (Bukhari 2519)"
"780","(780) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is sufficient to He does not repeat the washing of his head."
"781","(781) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: If a person in a state of impurity washes his head with marshmallow, that is sufficient. That, he said: And Abraham said the same thing, or he said: He will not repeat it."
"782","(782) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salem. And Hafs, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sariyah, and Sufyan did not mention Sariyah. He said: Abdullah was asked about sexual impurity. Should he wash his head with marshmallow? He said: It is sufficient for him if he washes himself, not to cut his head again."
"783","(783) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour bin Safiyyah, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; In a state of sexual impurity, he should wash his head with Sidr. He said: He should not wash his head."
"784","(784) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama; In a state of sexual impurity, he washes his head with marshmallow. He said: That is sufficient."
"785","(785) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muharrar ibn Qanab, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, in a similar vein."
"786","(786) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha al-Yami; He used to wash himself from ritual impurity in the house he used to stay in."
"787","(787) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri about a man whose ritual impurity afflicts him, and he has water with him. Is it sufficient for ablution? He said: He performs tayammum. Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah said: He performs ablution and performs tayammum."
"788","(788) Muhammad ibn Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he becomes in a state of impurity and does not have as much water as he needs to wash himself. With it, he said: He performs tayammum."
"789","(789) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; About a man taking a bath from ritual impurity, and his vessel was splashed with water, so he said: There is no harm in it."
"790","(790) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Muhammad: Should I bathe and have some of my washing sprinkled in my vessel? He said: Do you find anything better than that?"
"791","(791) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was asked about a man who takes a bath from ritual impurity and some of his washing drips into his vessel? He said: There is no harm in it."
"792","(792) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He was asked about a man who takes a bath and then sprinkles some of his washing in his vessel? He said: Can he refrain from this?"
"793","(793) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muammar bin Musa, on the authority of Abu Ja’far. And on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; He saw nothing wrong with washing himself in his vessel."
"794","(794) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: I said to Al-Zuhri: I should wash myself from impurity and cleanse myself of the impurity. Did I wash in my vessel? He said: There is no harm in it."
"795","(795) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Hussam bin Misk, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man asked Abu Huraira, there is an Ethiopian in him. He said: Should I wash myself and have some of my body return to my vessel? He said: There is no harm in it."
"796","(796) Waki’ informed us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Yahya ibn Atiq, he said: I asked Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin about A man takes a bath and exudes water from his washing into his vessel? Al-Hasan said: Who has the power to spread water? And Ibn Sirin said: Indeed, we hope for the mercy of our Lord, which is greater than this."
"797","(797) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Musa, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’ On the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, there is a woman who braids her head tightly, should I undo it to wash the janabah? He said: It is enough for you to throw three liters of water over it, then pour some water over yourself and be cleansed. Or: Then you have become pure. (Muslim 259. Ibn Majah 603)"
"798","(798) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: It was reported to Aisha that Abdullah bin Amr ordered the women, when they took a bath, to lower their heads. She said: What a strange thing this son of Amr is. Isn’t it? They ordered them to shave their heads! The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I used to wash from one vessel, so I did not do more than pour it on my head. Three voids. (Muslim 260. Ibn Majah 604)"
"799","(799) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say: The bride looses her hair when She wanted to wash."
"800","(800) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Uthman ibn Mawhib, on the authority of a woman who complained to Aisha about the washing The impurity, and she said: He was born three, so whatever he did right, he did right, and whatever he made a mistake, he made a mistake."
"801","(801) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir; A woman asked Umm Salama, and she said: Have three children, and she said: My hair is a lot, and she said: Lay some of it on top of the other."
"802","(802) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Salamah ibn Wahram, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: The comb is divided into three parts."
"803","(803) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Umm Salamah; She asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: I am a woman with a very braided head, so what should I do? Did you wash? He said: Give me a hug on your head three times, then give me a wink after each dip. (Abu Dawud 256)"
"804","(804) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri and Ata’ that they said: Do not let her hair relax, but Pour three times, then rub it."
"805","(805) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In a woman taking a bath, he said: Three handfuls are sufficient, and if she wishes, she should not untie her hair."
"806","(806) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Hammad about a woman when she takes a bath? He said: If she thinks that the water has hit her, that is sufficient for her, and if she thinks that the water has not hit her, then she can break it. And he said: The ruling: Its roots and its ends are wet and not destroyed."
"807","(807) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The menstruating woman and the one who is in a state of sexual intercourse are sexually active. Water is upon their heads, and it will not be stopped."
"808","(808) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Hudhafi, he said: He said to his wife: Mix your head with water, do not mix it with a little fire that remains on it."
"809","(809) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah al-Qardawani, on the authority of Ata’ and al-Zuhri. They said: Washing after menstruation. And the impurity is one."
"810","(810) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’; The wives of Ibn Umar and the mothers of his children used to wash themselves after impurity and menstruation and did not lower their heads, but They exaggerate their calamities."
"811","(811) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Ikrimah; He was asked about a woman who takes a bath after impurity and menstruation? He said: Let the strands loosen, and pour water over their heads until the roots of the hair are wet, but do not cause them to fall off."
"812","(812) Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: With her fingers. Ataa said the same."
"813","(813) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If one is in a state of impurity, it is sufficient for him to immerse himself in water."
"814","(814) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Ramsah is sufficient."
"815","(815) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Ramsah is sufficient."
"816","(816) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, on the authority of Shu`aib, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, who said: It suffices for one who is in a state of sexual impurity. If he dives deeply and touches it with his hand."
"817","(817) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Muslim, he said: I asked Ikrimah, he said: I told him: The junub is immersed. In the case of the ring, is that sufficient for ritual ablution? He said: Yes."
"818","(818) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Is he immersed in the water on the side? He said: It is sufficient."
"819","(819) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he entered the river, he rushed It is sufficient for it."
"820","(820) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim, Ata`, and Aamir. They said: Junub when he immerses himself in water immediately. Its parts"
"821","(821) Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Asam Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Ibn Budil ibn Warqa’, who said: I heard Al-Qasim say in the state of junub. He immersed himself in the water completely, saying: If he dangles you, that is sufficient."
"822","(822) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: A Ramsayah suffices for one who is in a state of impurity."
"823","(823) Ibn Mubarak and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, who said: Abu Ad-Duha was asked, “Does he eat?” The side? He said: Yes, and he walked in the markets."
"824","(824) Abdă bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: I am in a state of sexual impurity, so I perform ablution, then I go out to the market and relieve myself."
"825","(825) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who is impure and then wants to leave, he said: He performs ablution as he does for prayer."
"826","(826) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; About the junub man, the pilgrim comes and the market comes? He said: He washes his private parts, and performs his ablution for prayer."
"827","(827) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, similar to that."
"828","(828) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad; Perhaps he was in a state of impurity, then he performed ablution, then he left."
"829","(829) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi; Omar used to warm himself with his wife after washing."
"830","(830) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, she said: He was Abu al-Darda’. He takes a bath, then he comes and has a chickadee to warm himself with."
"831","(831) Hafs and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Jabalah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I wash myself from ritual impurity, then Iron the woman before she bathes."
"832","(832) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: That is the life of the Quraysh in the winter."
"833","(833) Ismail Ibn Aliya narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abu Kathir narrated to me, he said: I said to Abu Hurairah: Should a man wash himself from ritual impurity, then lie down with his family? He said: No problem."
"834","(834) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, who said: The black man used to avoid So he takes a bath, then his family comes and lies with her and warms himself up with her before she takes a bath."
"835","(835) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Alqamiya used to wash himself, then he would warm himself in the mirror. Side"
"836","(836) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; He used to warm himself with his wife, then he would get up and perform his ablution for prayer."
"837","(837) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He used to take a bath from ritual impurity, then he would come and warm himself with his wife before she took a bath, then he would pray and not He touches water."
"838","(838) Abu Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a person in a state of ritual ablution takes a bath, then he intends to To have intercourse with his wife, he may do so if he wishes."
"839","(839) Abu Khalid Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: He engages in it but not He has ablution."
"840","(840) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in him warming his wife after washing."
"841","(841) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad; He used to hate it until it dried up."
"842","(842) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he takes a bath from the ritual impurity, then he warms himself with me before I take a bath. (Ibn Majah 580, Tirmidhi 123)"
"843","(843) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a woman’s abstinence, then menstruation. He said: She takes a bath."
"844","(844) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Menstruation is more severe than impurity."
"845","(845) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said: Concerning a man who afflicts his wife, then she menstruates before she takes a bath. He said: Anas used to like for her to take a bath."
"846","(846) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri; Concerning a man who had intercourse with his wife; So she had her period before she took a bath. He said: She takes a bath."
"847","(847) Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a woman avoiding menstruation, then she menstruates? They said: You take a bath."
"848","(848) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, who said: You take a bath."
"849","(849) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She takes a bath, then she remains menstruating."
"850","(850) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Ata’, he said: She does not have to wash, he said: And Hammad said, on the authority of Ibrahim: She must wash."
"851","(851) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about avoiding a woman, then Do you menstruate before you take a bath? He said: If she menstruates, then it is her right to bathe."
"852","(852) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Amer, who said: If she wishes, she may wash, and if she wishes, she may not wash."
"853","(853) Muhammad bin Maysar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: She washes herself from impurity, so when she is pure, she washes herself from impurity. Menstruation"
"854","(854) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If he has a dream and does not see wetness, then no ghusl is required of him. If he sees wetness and does not see that he has had a wet dream, then he must perform ablution."
"855","(855) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, he said: While I was riding on my camel, and I was between sleep and wakefulness When I found something bad, I denied myself, and water came out from me, and wet urine, and what was there, so I asked Ibn Abbas? He said: Wash your penis and whatever is on your part, but he did not command me to wash. (Abdul Razzaq 609)"
"856","(856) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he woke up and saw that he had intercourse, he did not see any wetness. There is no washing on him."
"857","(857) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same way."
"858","(858) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, similar to that."
"859","(859) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of Ali bin Thabit, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He was asked about a man who woke up from his dream and saw trouble? He said: If I had found that, I would have washed myself with it."
"860","(860) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who finds wetness after sleeping, he said: He should take a bath."
"861","(861) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; He said: He should not wash himself until he is certain that he has committed a state of ritual impurity."
"862","(862) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr and Ata’, who said: If he sees wetness, let him wash himself."
"863","(863) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who wakes up and finds calamity? Al-Hakam said: He should not take a bath, and Hammad said: If he thinks that he has had a wet dream, then he should take a bath."
"864","(864) Waki’ told us, he said: I heard Sufyan say: He takes a bath."
"865","(865) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mu’ammar, on the authority of his followers, who said: He does not wash until he is confident."
"866","(866) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: Washing from lust and period."
"867","(867) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who wakes up in the morning and sees wetness on his head. He said: If he thinks that he has a wet dream, then he should wash himself, but if he does not see it, then he should wash. He had a wet dream and did not wash himself.\n His leaders said: If it is flowing water, he has washed himself. So I said to his leaders: How does he know? He said: He smells it, and the arbiter said: He does not take a bath."
"868","(868) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Amri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: If one of you wakes up and sees wetness, but does not see that he has had a wet dream, then he should bathe. He had a wet dream and did not see any wetness, so he did not have to wash himself. (Ahmad 2561, Abu Dawud 640)"
"869","(869) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Safiyy ibn Shaybab, on the authority of Aisha, who said: She entered The names of his sons were in disgrace to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: O Messenger of God, how can one of us wash when she is pure? From menstruation? He said: She takes her lotion and water, performs ablution, washes her head, and massages it until the water reaches the roots of her hair, then She poured water over her body, then took her time and purified herself with it, and said: O Messenger of God, how should I purify myself with it? He said: Purify yourself with it. Aisha said: Then I knew what he told me about it, so I said to her: Follow traces of blood. (Bukhari 314) Muslim 61)"
"870","(870) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her during her menstruation: Let your hair comb and take a bath. (Ibn Majah 641)"
"871","(871) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ammarah bin Ruwaybah, on the authority of a woman, on the authority of Umm She said: If she is one of us, then when she takes a bath after ritual impurity, she will leave her braids intact."
"872","(872) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin; He was asked about a heavy woman, or a large woman whose hand does not reach her back when washing from impurity, or menstruation? He said: We hope for God’s mercy which is greater than this."
"873","(873) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Dinar, he said: I said to Al-Hasan: The foreign slave woman does not wash well. He said : Order her to wipe her forehead with a rag and wash herself with water inside and out, and perform the ablution she does for prayer, then take a bath."
"874","(874) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If one of you has intercourse with his family during the night, then wants to return, let him perform ablution between them.\n(Abu Dawud 222. Tirmidhi 141)"
"875","(875) Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman bin Rabi’i, who said: Omar said to me: O Salman. ! If you came to your family and then wanted to come back, what would you do? I said: How should I do? He said: Perform ablution between them."
"876","(876) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’; When Ibn Umar came to his family and then wanted to return, he would wash his face and arms."
"877","(877) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muharib, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: If she wants to perform ablution again, she should perform ablution."
"878","(878) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not think there was anything wrong with a man having intercourse with his wife and then coming back before he had performed ablution. He said: It was Ibn Sirin. He says: I don't know of any harm in that. He said: That was said because it was better for him to return."
"879","(879) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Walid Al-Shinni, who said: I heard Ikrimah saying: If she wants him to return, she should perform ablution."
"880","(880) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Arif bin Dirham, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He performs ablution."
"881","(881) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he wants to perform ablution again, he performs ablution."
"882","(882) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Muharbibi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If he wants to perform ablution again, he performs ablution."
"883","(883) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama, she said: Umm Sulaim came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about the woman who sees in her dreams, what does the man see? He said: If she sees water, let her wash herself. So I said to her: Women have exposed themselves, and does a woman have a wet dream? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Let your right hand be dusted, so your children will resemble it. (Bukhari 1300, Muslim 251)"
"884","(884) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that Umm Sulaym asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of a woman who sees in her dreams what a man sees? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If she sees that and ejaculates, then she must wash. Umm Salama said: O Messenger of God. By God, can I be this? He said: Yes, a man’s semen is thick and white, and a woman’s semen is thin and yellow, so whichever is above, or above, is more like a child.\n(Muslim 30. An-Nasa’i 202)"
"885","(885) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Khawla bint Hakim; She asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a woman who sees in her dreams what a man sees? He said: She does not have to wash until she ejaculates, just as a man does not have to wash until he ejaculates. (Ahmad 6/409. Ibn Majah 602)"
"886","(886) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Amir narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: A woman, who was called a woman, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, one of us Do you see that she is with her husband in a dream? He said: If you find moisture, take a bath, O beautiful one."
"887","(887) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ata’ and Abu Salma bin Abdul Rahman. And Mujahid said: Umm Sulaim said: O Messenger of God! A woman sees in her dreams what a man sees, is she obligated to perform ablution? He said: Do you find anything? She said: Maybe! He said: Do you find any moisture? She said: Maybe! He said: Let her wash herself. Then some women met her and said to her: You have exposed us in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: By God, I would not stop until I knew what was permissible or what was forbidden."
"888","(888) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid; He said: If a woman falls asleep and sees what a man sees, then she should bathe."
"889","(889) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, he said: I asked about him. Safe, striving, and giving. They said: She should wash herself if she sees what a man sees."
"890","(890) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Abraham used to deny women’s wet dreams."
"891","(891) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: If a woman sees what a man sees Let her take a bath."
"892","(892) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ma’rif, on the authority of Ismail ibn Raja’i, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She does not have to wash, and he said Atom you wash."
"893","(893) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Sabara, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha; He said: Ali was asked about a woman who sees in her dreams what a man sees. Should she bathe? He said: Yes, if she sees the wetness."
"894","(894) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: When she saw A woman is what a man sees. Then she came down and took a bath."
"895","(895) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If she sees water, let her bathe."
"896","(896) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, he said: If a woman sees What a man sees, let him wash himself."
"897","(897) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan Dirar, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever scoops water while he is junub. Whatever remains of it is unclean, and angels do not enter a house in which there is urine."
"898","(898) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In junub, he puts his hand into the vessel before washing it, or a man gets up from his dream and puts his hand into the vessel. Before he washed her, he said: If he wants, he can perform ablution, and if he wants, he can excrete it."
"899","(899) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of someone who heard Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab say: There is no harm in dipping The junub person puts his hand in the vessel before he washes it."
"900","(900) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Aisha bin Sa’d, who said: Sa’d was in charge of his female servant. So she takes the bird from the water to him, dips her hand in it, and it is said: She is menstruating! So he says: Her menstruation is not in her hand."
"901","(901) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: They were the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They put their hands into the vessel while they are in the state of menstruation, and the women while they are menstruating, and they see no harm in that, meaning: Before they washed her."
"902","(902) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If a man commits sexual impurity while wearing his clothes. If he sees any traces on it, let him wash it, but if he does not see any traces on it, let him sprinkle it."
"903","(903) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: A man from the neighborhood said to Abu Misra: I am committing junub while wearing my clothes. So I look and see nothing? He said: When you have washed yourself, wrap yourself in it while you are wet, that will be sufficient for you."
"904","(904) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. ; He used to say regarding ritual impurity on a garment: If you see traces of it, wash it, and if you know that it got on it, then hide it. You have to wash the garment, and if you are in doubt and do not know whether the garment is dirty or not, then sprinkle it over it."
"905","(905) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If it is hidden from him His place and knowing that he had done it, he washed the entire garment."
"906","(906) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zayd ibn al-Salt; Omar bin Al-Khattab washed what he saw, sprinkled what he did not see, and repeated it after he became strong."
"907","(907) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Sari bin Yahya, on the authority of Abdul Karim bin Rashid, on the authority of Anas; Concerning a man who was in a state of impurity in his garment and did not see any traces of it, he said: He should wash it completely."
"908","(908) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab; Regarding ritual impurity, in the garment, he said: If you see it, wash it, and if you go astray, sprinkle it."
"909","(909) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; In the case of a man, he covers his janabah garment, then hides in front of him? He said: Wash it all."
"910","(910) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; About a man who has a wet dream while wearing a garment but does not know where it is? He said: The garment is soaked with water."
"911","(911) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Douching only makes it worse."
"912","(912) Mahboub Al-Qawariri narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Habib, on the authority of Salem, who said: A man asked him and he said: I had a wet dream. My dress? He said: Wash it. He said: Is it hidden from me? He said: Sprinkle him with water."
"913","(913) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He should not sprinkle it with water."
"914","(914) Yazeed bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, he said: Saeed bin Ubaid bin Al-Sabbaq told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Sahil bin Hanif, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, what about what gets on my dress? He said: A handful of water is sufficient for you to sprinkle on your garment wherever you see that it has reached it. (Ahmad 485. Abu Dawud 212)"
"915","(915) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, who said: I said to Sa’id bin Jubayr: I have a wet dream in my garment. He said: If I find it So wash him, or else let him go. He said: I said: Should I throw him away and wear another garment? He said: You have many blankets."
"916","(916) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Regarding ritual impurity, in the garment, he said: If you see it, wash it, and if you do not see it, then leave it, and do not sprinkle water on it, for sprinkling is not Yazidah is nothing but filthy."
"917","(917) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal bin Maimoon, who said: I asked Ata bin Yazid Al-Laythi about sexual impurity. Are you in the dress? He said: Sprinkle it with water."
"918","(918) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: I asked Sulaiman ibn Yasar about the garment that causes it. Semen, should he wash it or wash the entire garment? Suleiman said: Aisha said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to tie his garment and wash it from his garment. Then he goes out in his dress to pray, and I see the effect of washing on it. (Bukhari 229. Muslim 239)"
"919","(919) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Ibn Masoud used to wash the traces of a wet dream from his clothes."
"920","(920) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Wash the semen from your clothes."
"921","(921) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zubaid; Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him, washed away what he saw."
"922","(922) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: You saw me finding him. In the garment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I covered it for him. It means semen. (Abu Dawud 375. Muslim 239)"
"923","(923) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’d; He was rubbing the side of his garment."
"924","(924) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad; He was rubbing the side of his garment."
"925","(925) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, who said: A guest came to Aisha, and she commanded him. With a yellow blanket, so he had a wet dream in it, so he was ashamed to send traces of a wet dream on it, so he dipped it in water, then He sent for her, and Aisha said: Why did he spoil our dress? It was enough for him to rub it with his finger. Perhaps I rubbed it from the garment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. With my two fingers (Tirmidhi 1161, Muslim 106)"
"926","(926) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: While we were with Abdullah bin Omar after he had prayed, He showed you his garment, and said: I looked for this yesterday but did not find it. Mujahid said: I see nothing but semen."
"927","(927) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, Sa’d bin Tariq, who said: I said to Al-Sha’abi: I have arrived in the morning. Is your dress shiny? He said: I will lick it, then shake it off. He said: I said: Should I wash it? He said: It makes it stink. Abu Malik said: I thought that if it had been wet, he would have ordered it to be washed."
"928","(928) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning semen, he said: Wipe it with your penis."
"929","(929) Hushaym told us, he said: Hajjaj and Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Regarding ritual impurity, it touches the garment. He said: It is only like palm tree, or marrow. Wipe it off from yourself with a rag, or With your remembrance"
"930","(930) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: If it is dry, eat it."
"931","(931) Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning sexual impurity, he refers to the garment, he said: he washes it, or wipes it with his Ikhdirah."
"932","(932) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami; He sent a message to Aisha asking her about the opportunity for a man to have intercourse with her, whether he would read the Qur’an to her? She said: What prevents you from that? If you see it, wash it, if you want, scrub it, and if it gets wet, brush it."
"933","(933) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Ezza, who said: A man asked Omar bin Al-Khattab and he said: : Did I have a wet dream about myself? He said: If it is wet, wash it, and if it is dry, rub it, and if it is difficult for you, sprinkle it."
"934","(934) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zayd Ibn Jud’an, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he sits among the four people, and then makes circumcision attach to circumcision, then it is obligatory Washing (Ahmad 6/1351 Tirmidhi 109)"
"935","(935) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: If circumcision exceeds circumcision It is obligatory to wash, as this was from me and from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we would wash with him.\n(Ahmad 6/161, Tirmidhi 108)"
"936","(936) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: If he sits among its four people, then struggles with them, he will It is obligatory to wash. (Bukhari 291. Muslim 87)"
"937","(937) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Yunus said: I do not know him unless he has He raised him, saying: If he sits between her four private parts, then he strives, it is obligatory to wash him, whether he ejaculates or not."
"938","(938) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ali, who said: If the two circumcisions meet, then washing is obligatory."
"939","(939) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzali al-Jumahi, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Umar said: If a man mixes with his family It is obligatory to wash."
"940","(940) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Aisha said: If the two circumcisions meet, then it is obligatory Washing"
"941","(941) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, and on the authority of Nafi’. They said: She said: Aisha: If circumcision violates circumcision, then it is obligatory to wash."
"942","(942) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Habib ibn Shihab, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Hurairah said: If the rounded word is absent It is obligatory to wash."
"943","(943) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: As for me, when I reach That is where she took a bath."
"944","(944) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of Ghalib Abi Al-Dhail, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, said: If circumcision exceeds circumcision, then ghusl is obligatory."
"945","(945) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Bukair ibn Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Saeed ibn Al-Musayyab, who said: Omar said: No. A man was brought to him who did it, meaning: he had intercourse and then did not ejaculate or wash himself, except that I cursed him as a punishment."
"946","(946) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: The immigrants gathered; Abu Bakr, Omar, Othman, and Ali; That what necessitates flogging, and stoning necessitates washing."
"947","(947) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I heard him say: Killing and stoning are obligatory, but they are not obligatory. A vessel of water?"
"948","(948) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Shurayh said: Is four thousand obligatory, but not a vessel? From water? Meaning: the one who mixes with others and then does not come down."
"949","(949) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Shurayh said: Four thousand is obligatory, but it is not obligatory. A vessel of water? Meaning: the one who mixes with others and then does not come down."
"950","(950) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I asked Ubaydah: What makes ghusl necessary? He said: Mixing and streaming."
"951","(951) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun and Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, the same."
"952","(952) Abdul-Ala bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Muammar bin Abi Huyya, the client of his son Safwan, on the authority of Ubaid bin Rifa’i bin Rafi’, on the authority of his father Rifa’i bin Rafi’; He said: While I was with Omar ibn al-Khattab, a man entered and said: O Commander of the Faithful, this is Zayd ibn Thabit. The people in the mosque were given a fatwa with their opinion regarding washing one’s body from impurity, so Omar said: I have to do it, so Zaid came, and when Omar saw him, he said O enemy of his own soul, have you reached the point of issuing fatwas to people with your opinion? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, for God’s sake, I did not do it, but I heard a hadith from my uncles, so I narrated it. From Abi Ayyub, from Ubayy bin Ka’b, and from Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, so Umar approached Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ and said: He has Did you do that? If one of you came to the mirror and became lazy, he did not perform ablution? He said: We used to do that at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but no prohibition came to us from God regarding it. There was no prohibition from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Does he know that? He said: I do not know. So Omar ordered the gathering of the Muhajireen and Ansar, and they gathered for him. He consulted with them, and the people advised that there should be no ghusl. That is, except for the case of Muadh and Ali, for they said: If circumcision exceeds circumcision, then it is obligatory to wash, so Omar said: This And you were the companions of Badr, and you disagreed, but after you there will be more disagreement. He said: Then Ali said: O Commander of the Faithful, No one knows more about this than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than his wives. So he sent for Hafs She said: I have no knowledge of this, so he sent for Aisha and she said: If circumcision passes beyond circumcision, then washing is required. Omar said: I do not listen. If a man does that, I will punish him with a beating. (Ahmad 5/115)"
"953","(953) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Saif bin Wahhab, on the authority of Abi Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad Al-Daili, On the authority of Umairah bin Yathribi, on the authority of Ubayy, who said: If their two joints meet after circumcision, washing is obligatory."
"954","(954) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid. He said: I asked Zayd bin Thabit about a man who has intercourse and then does not ejaculate? He said: He has to wash. He said: I told him: My father did not see that, so he said: My father refrained from that before... He dies"
"955","(955) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: As for me, if I mix My family, I took a bath."
"956","(956) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If circumcision exceeds circumcision, ghusl is obligatory."
"957","(957) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sahl ibn Sa’d, who said: The Ansar’s saying was: water is from Water: It was a concession at the beginning of Islam, then washing was done after that."
"958","(958) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla; He heard it from Omar, or from his brother. He heard it from Omar. He said: If circumcision passes beyond circumcision, then ghusl is obligatory."
"959","(959) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Shami, who said: I heard al-Nu’man bin Bashir say; Concerning a man who is lazy and does not ejaculate, he said: He should take a bath."
"960","(960) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Hanzali, who said: Al-Qasim was told: The Ansar do not bathe except with water, so he said : But we seek refuge in God lest we do that."
"961","(961) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If the two circumcisions meet and the penis is hidden, then ghusl is obligatory. (Ahmad 2/178 Ibn Majah 611)"
"962","(962) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yassar, on the authority of Zayd ibn Khalid al-Janni; He asked five of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they all said: A water is from a water, among them is Ali ibn Ubayy. Student"
"963","(963) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of a man from the people of Jadr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Water from water."
"964","(964) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah said: Water is from water."
"965","(965) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sulaym bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He said: Water is from water."
"966","(966) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man from the Ansar, so he sent for him, and he came out with his head dripping, and he said: Perhaps we Did we hasten you? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: If you are pregnant or have an abortion, then you have to perform ablution, but you do not have to wash. (Bukhari 1801) Ahmad 3/21)"
"967","(967) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Kharsha bin Habib, on the authority of Ali, He said regarding ghusl after intercourse, if he did not ejaculate, then he did not perform ghusl? It was said: And if he shakes him with it? He said: Even if he shakes her with it until it shakes her earrings."
"968","(968) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I heard Hilal speaking, on the authority of Al-Murqi’, on the authority of the mother of a son of Sa’d ibn Abi Waqqas; That Saad used to come to her, so if he did not come down, he did not take a bath."
"969","(969) Suwayd bin Amr told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ayoub, On the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: There is nothing in idleness except birds.\n(Ahmad 5/113. Bukhari 293)"
"970","(970) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama; That Ata bin Yassar told him, that Zayd bin Khalid Al-Janni told him, that he asked Othman bin Affan, he said: I said: Have you seen if a man has intercourse with a woman and does not menstruate? Othman said: He performs ablution as one does for prayer, and washes his penis. Othman said: I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: I asked Ali, Al-Zubayr, Talhah, and Ubayy ibn Ka’b about that, and they ordered him to do so.\n(Bukhari 1791, Muslim 270)"
"971","(971) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla told me, on the authority of Ali. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about madhiy? He said: In it is ablution, and in semen is washing. (Tirmidhi 114, Ahmad 121)"
"972","(972) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, who said: I was finding madhiy, so I ordered Al-Miqdad to He asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, because I had his daughter, so I was ashamed to ask him, so he asked him, and he said: Every male stallion undergoes pre-ejaculation, so if it is pre-emission, then ritual bathing is required, and if it is pre-emission, then ablution is required."
"973","(973) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Al-Hanafiyyah, who said: I heard him narrating, on the authority of his father On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar hadith of Al-Hasan. (Bukhari 132. Muslim 18)"
"974","(974) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Shaybah, on the authority of Abu Habib bin Ali bin Minya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He came to Ubayyah and Omar was with him, so he came out to them and said: I found some madness, so I washed my penis and performed ablution, so Omar said: Or Is that sufficient for you? He said: Yes, he said: Did you hear it from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. (Ibn Majah 507)"
"975","(975) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Mushir, on the authority of Kharsha ibn Al-Hurr, who said: Omar was asked about madhiyyah. ? He said: That is breaking the fast, and part of it is ablution."
"976","(976) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymiyy, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, that Salman ibn Rabi‘ah married A woman from Banu Aqeel saw her and played with her. He said: Then came out of her what comes out of a man - Sulayman said: Or he said: precum. - He said: So I took a bath, then I came to Omar and asked him? He said: You do not have to perform ghusl for that, that is spreading."
"977","(977) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Sa’id bin Ubaid bin Al-Subaq narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asked by Ibn Hanif, he said: I was vomiting a lot of precum, so I used to bathe frequently, so I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and he said: Only ablution is sufficient for you for that."
"978","(978) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Anas Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Abbas said: Semen is to be washed away from it. He washes his private parts and performs ablution with pre-ejaculatory fluid, and I do not know what it is from lust."
"979","(979) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of his uncle Abu Al-Muhallab, he said: He was one of his family. A person was taking a bath with what comes out after urination, and he said to him: But ablution suffices for it."
"980","(980) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: I do not know what it is from lust."
"981","(981) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They mentioned, according to Ibn Umar, calamity, madhiyah, and some The man found it and said: You remember something that I cannot find, and if I had found it, I would have washed myself with it."
"982","(982) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Abd Rabbah bin Musa, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Maniy is one of the means of washing, and madhiy and watery water are to be performed as ablution."
"983","(983) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He was asked about madhiy? He said: That is the activity, which includes ablution."
"984","(984) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Istabraq, who said: I asked Salim about madhiy? He said: He should perform ablution from it."
"985","(985) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan and Umar ibn al-Walid al-Shinni, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Maniy and al-Wadiyyah As for madhiy, as for semen, it is ablution, and as for madhiy and watery water, it involves washing one’s penis and performing ablution."
"986","(986) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, he said: I said to Al-Hasan Al-Basri: Have you seen a man, if he knows what he does? He said: Every stallion will gestate, so if that happens, let him wash his penis."
"987","(987) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Maniy, watery water, and precum, so in semen is washing. And the valley and the madhiy are ablution."
"988","(988) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr; He said regarding pre-eclampsia: He washes the penis three times and performs ablution."
"989","(989) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Semen and al-Wady As for pre-eclampsia, as for semen, it is ablution, and as for pre-madhiy and watery water, it is ablution, and the penis is washed."
"990","(990) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Husayn bin Qubaysiyya Al-Fazariy, on the authority of Ali He said: I was a man who had a sexual intercourse, and the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was under my bed, so I was ashamed to ask him. So I ordered a man to ask him? He said: If you see precum, perform ablution and wash your penis, and if you see water gushing out, then wash your penis.\n(Ahmad 1/1258 An-Nasa’i 200)"
"991","(991) Ubaidah bin Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Husayn bin Qubaysah, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; In the same way (Abu Dawud 208 and Ibn Hibban 1107)"
"992","(992) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydi, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace; In the same way (Bukhari 269. Ahmad 1/125)"
"993","(993) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Shubayl, he said: Ali said: I was a man who had a bath, so whenever I saw any of that, I would wash myself, and that was reported to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he ordered me to perform ablution."
"994","(994) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’; As for what a woman gets from her husband’s semen, she should wash it, and she should not wash it unless the water enters her private parts. If it enters Let her take a bath."
"995","(995) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife without her private part, he said: He washes and she washes her private part, unless she ejaculates."
"996","(996) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; Concerning a man who has a wet dream while his wife is next to him, and some of his water falls on her. She does not have to wash, and she may wash wherever she is. He touches her, unless he touches her private parts, in which case she should bathe."
"997","(997) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Firas, who said: I bought a young slave girl, and I was more likely to suffer from her than anyone else. Other than mixing with her, she asked Al-Shaabi? He said: As for you, take a bath. As for her, ablution is sufficient for her."
"998","(998) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who has intercourse with a woman other than her private parts. He said: If she ejaculates, she has bathed, but if she does not ejaculate, She performed ablution and washed off the man’s semen that had gotten on her body."
"999","(999) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: She wipes her private parts and performs ablution. If it was dirty blood on her, she bathed and was intimate with herself, then it was an attack from Satan, so if she did that, it became bitter, or Twice he went."
"1000","(1000) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: When she saw A woman after she purifies herself from menstruation, like a meat-washing woman, or a woman’s blood clot, or more than that, or less than that. So let her sprinkle water, then perform ablution and pray, and do not wash unless you see dirty blood, for it is only a run from Satan. In the womb"
"1001","(1001) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abbad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, she said: She was Aisha forbids women from looking at themselves during menstruation at night, and says: It may be yellowness. And trouble"
"1002","(1002) Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the mirror \n You take a bath, then you see the yellow color. He said: You take a bath and pray."
